{"raw": {"https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Flinders-Rural-Health-SA-Mount-Gambier--On-the-Traditional-Lands-of-the-First-Nations-of-the-South-East/Casual-Professional-Academic-Register---Rural-and-Remote-Health-SA_JR0000011666-1": {"title": "Casual Professional/Academic Register \u2013 Rural and Remote Health SA", "description": "Posted: 2026-03-02\nPart time\n\nAbout Flinders Our bold ambition, articulated in our Strategic Plan Impact. With Purpose: The 2035 Agenda , is to change 10 million lives for the better by opening opportunities, solving real\u2011world problems, and translating knowledge into outcomes that strengthen communities. \u00a0 With a renewed focus on putting students first, being the university for industry and enterprise, and delivering research that creates meaningful impact, we recognise that exceptional people are central to our success. Casual Register Flinders Rural and Remote Health SA Flinders University Rural and Remote Health SA (FRRHSA) facilitates high quality multidisciplinary health education and research in our State's regional areas. We have a strong national and international reputation for providing community-engaged inter-professional training for medical, nursing, and allied health students. This includes the Doctor of Medicine Rural Stream (MDRS) program and multidisciplinary rural clinical placements. Casual Register Flinders University has a number of Casual Registers as a means of expressions of interest for the purpose of casual work, should such opportunities arise. This casual register applies specifically to our Rural and Remote Health SA Campuses. These campuses include: Mount Gambier Murray Bridge Nuriootpa Renmark Victor Harbor How to Register: Upload your current CV/Resume detailing your qualifications and experience You may choose to upload a Cover Letter of no more than 1 page to support your CV/Resume Your application will be acknowledged by an automated e-mail once submitted. If a casual opportunity is available and your application is considered suitable, the relevant hiring manager will contact you for a further discussion. Please note, only suitable applicants will be contacted. Applying to the Casual Register does not guarantee employment. Further Information: Pursuant to Child Safety (Prohibited Persons) Act 2016 (SA) this position may be deemed prescribed.\u00a0It is an inherent requirement of a prescribed position that the successful candidate maintains a current Working With Children Check which is satisfactory to the University Please contact Recruitment@Flinders\u00a0by email at recruitment@flinders.edu.au \u00a0should you have any queries regarding Casual opportunities."}, "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Bedford-Park/Casual-Academic-Register---College-of-Business-Government-and-Law_JR0000000087": {"title": "Casual Academic Register \u2013 College of Business, Creative Arts, Law and Social Sciences", "description": "Posted: 2026-02-26\nPart time\n\nAbout Flinders Our bold ambition, articulated in our Strategic Plan Impact. With Purpose: The 2035 Agenda , is to change 10 million lives for the better by opening opportunities, solving real\u2011world problems, and translating knowledge into outcomes that strengthen communities. \u00a0 With a renewed focus on putting students first, being the university for industry and enterprise, and delivering research that creates meaningful impact, we recognise that exceptional people are central to our success. Casual Register Flinders University has a number of Casual Registers as a means of expressions of interest for the purpose of casual work, should such opportunities arise. How to Register: Upload your current CV/Resum\u00e9 detailing your qualifications and experience. You may choose to upload a Cover Letter of no more than 1 page to support your CV/Resum\u00e9. Your application will be acknowledged by an automated e-mail once submitted. If a casual opportunity is available and your application is considered suitable, the relevant hiring manager will contact you for a further discussion. Please note, only suitable applicants will be contacted. Applying to the Casual Register does not guarantee employment. Further Information: Pursuant to Child Safety (Prohibited Persons) Act 2016 (SA) this position may be deemed prescribed.\u00a0 It is an inherent requirement of a prescribed position that the successful candidate maintains a current Working With Children Check which is satisfactory to the University. Please contact Recruitment@Flinders \u00a0by email at recruitment@flinders.edu.au \u00a0should you have any queries regarding Casual opportunities."}, "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Bedford-Park/Casual-Academic-Register---College-of-Education--Psychology-and-Social-Work_JR0000000085": {"title": "Casual Academic Register \u2013 College of Human Sciences and Culture", "description": "Posted: 2026-02-26\nPart time\n\nAbout Flinders Our bold ambition, articulated in our Strategic Plan Impact. With Purpose: The 2035 Agenda , is to change 10 million lives for the better by opening opportunities, solving real\u2011world problems, and translating knowledge into outcomes that strengthen communities. \u00a0 With a renewed focus on putting students first, being the university for industry and enterprise, and delivering research that creates meaningful impact, we recognise that exceptional people are central to our success. Casual Register Flinders University has a number of Casual Registers as a means of expressions of interest for the purpose of casual work, should such opportunities arise. How to Register: Upload your current CV/Resum\u00e9 detailing your qualifications and experience. You may choose to upload a Cover Letter of no more than 1 page to support your CV/Resum\u00e9. Your application will be acknowledged by an automated e-mail once submitted. If a casual opportunity is available and your application is considered suitable, the relevant hiring manager will contact you for a further discussion. Please note, only suitable applicants will be contacted. Applying to the Casual Register does not guarantee employment. Further Information: Pursuant to Child Safety (Prohibited Persons) Act 2016 (SA) this position may be deemed prescribed.\u00a0 It is an inherent requirement of a prescribed position that the successful candidate maintains a current Working With Children Check which is satisfactory to the University. Please contact Recruitment@Flinders \u00a0by email at recruitment@flinders.edu.au \u00a0should you have any queries regarding Casual opportunities."}, "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Centre-for-Remote-Health-Alice-Springs/Casual-Professional-Academic-Register---Rural-and-Remote-Health-NT_JR0000011671-1": {"title": "Casual Professional/Academic Register \u2013 Rural and Remote Health NT", "description": "Posted: 2026-02-26\nPart time\n\nAbout Flinders Our bold ambition, articulated in our Strategic Plan Impact. With Purpose: The 2035 Agenda , is to change 10 million lives for the better by opening opportunities, solving real\u2011world problems, and translating knowledge into outcomes that strengthen communities. \u00a0 With a renewed focus on putting students first, being the university for industry and enterprise, and delivering research that creates meaningful impact, we recognise that exceptional people are central to our success. Casual Register Flinders Rural and Remote Health NT At \u00a0 Flinders Rural and Remote Health NT , our aim is to be a hub for innovative health research, education, and workforce development across the Northern Territory.\u00a0 We engage with students, community, and stakeholders to provide critical programs, such as the Northern Territory Medical Program, Paramedicine, Rural Clinical School, and the University Department of Rural Health. Our postgraduate education pathways (Remote Health Practice program), provides workforce development through Indigenous health and clinical skills training, and we have a community driven research program led by researchers committed to improving health outcomes. We work alongside Poche SA+NT focussing on Indigenous leadership capacity development and developing the Indigenous health workforce.\u00a0 All activities are driven by our values which focus on the long-term and short-term needs of the NT community. Casual Register Flinders University has a number of Casual Registers as a means of expressions of interest for the purpose of casual work, should such opportunities arise. This casual register applies specifically to our Rural and Remote Health NT Campuses. These campuses include: Alice Springs Darwin Katherine Nhulunbuy Tennant Creek How to Register: Upload your current CV/Resume detailing your qualifications and experience You may choose to upload a Cover Letter of no more than 1 page to support your CV/Resume Your application will be acknowledged by an automated e-mail once submitted. If a casual opportunity is available and your application is considered suitable, the relevant hiring manager will contact you for a further discussion. Please note, only suitable applicants will be contacted. Applying to the Casual Register does not guarantee employment. Further Information: Northern Territory Government legislation (the Care and Protection of Children Act 2007) now requires all individuals in child related employment or whose duties involve, or are likely to involve, contact with a child, to hold a valid \u2018Working with Children Clearance\u2019 (Ochre Card). This position involves child related work and is assessed as requiring a Working with Children Clearance/Ochre Card Please contact Recruitment@Flinders\u00a0by email at recruitment@flinders.edu.au \u00a0should you have any queries regarding Casual opportunities."}, "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Bedford-Park--Kaurna-Country/Casual-Professional-Register--Flinders-Students_JR0000012092": {"title": "Casual Professional Register - Flinders Students", "description": "Posted: 2026-02-26\nPart time\n\nAbout Flinders Our bold ambition, articulated in our Strategic Plan Impact. With Purpose: The 2035 Agenda , is to change 10 million lives for the better by opening opportunities, solving real\u2011world problems, and translating knowledge into outcomes that strengthen communities. \u00a0 With a renewed focus on putting students first, being the university for industry and enterprise, and delivering research that creates meaningful impact, we recognise that exceptional people are central to our success. Casual Register Flinders University has a range of casual job opportunities available for current students across its various campuses, including: Bedford Park Flinders City Campus Tonsley Flinders in the Northern Territory Flinders University operates year-round and requires casual employees to support events, projects, and the general day-to-day operations of the University. We value our students and are committed to offering opportunities that help them develop their skills, expand their capabilities, and foster meaningful relationships. If this opportunity interests you, we strongly encourage you to apply to our casual professional register. Please note, only students currently enrolled at the Flinders University are eligible to apply for this register. How does the Casual register work? Flinders University has a number of Casual Registers as a means of expressions of interest for the purpose of casual work, should such opportunities arise. We recognise the key to our success is exceptional people and we welcome registrations of interest from current Flinders students wishing to join our team on a casual or short-term basis. If a casual opportunity is available and your application is considered suitable, the relevant hiring manager will contact you for a further discussion. Applying to the Casual Register does not guarantee employment. How to Apply and Information: Upload your current CV detailing your qualifications and experience. You may choose to upload a Cover Letter of no more than 1 page to support your CV/Resum\u00e9. Please contact Recruitment@Flinders\u00a0by email at recruitment@flinders.edu.au \u00a0should you have any queries regarding casual opportunities. Prescribed Conditions for Employment (If Applicable): You may be required to provide a valid Nationally Coordinated Criminal History Check which is satisfactory to the University. You may be required to provide a current Working With Children Check which is satisfactory to the University in accordance with the Child Safety (Prohibited Persons) Act 2016 (SA)."}, "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Bedford-Park/Casual-Professional-Register---Curriculum-Impact_JR0000010615": {"title": "Casual Professional Register \u2013 Curriculum Impact", "description": "Posted: 2026-02-26\nPart time\n\nAbout Flinders Our bold ambition, articulated in our Strategic Plan Impact. With Purpose: The 2035 Agenda , is to change 10 million lives for the better by opening opportunities, solving real\u2011world problems, and translating knowledge into outcomes that strengthen communities. \u00a0 With a renewed focus on putting students first, being the university for industry and enterprise, and delivering research that creates meaningful impact, we recognise that exceptional people are central to our success. Casual Register Flinders University has a number of Casual Registers as a means of expressions of interest for the purpose of casual work, should such opportunities arise. How to Register: Upload your current CV/Resum\u00e9 detailing your qualifications and experience. You may choose to upload a Cover Letter of no more than 1 page to support your CV/Resum\u00e9. Your application will be acknowledged by an automated e-mail once submitted. If a casual opportunity is available and your application is considered suitable, the relevant hiring manager will contact you for a further discussion. Please note, only suitable applicants will be contacted. Applying to the Casual Register does not guarantee employment. Further Information: Pursuant to Child Safety (Prohibited Persons) Act 2016 (SA) this position may be deemed prescribed.\u00a0 It is an inherent requirement of a prescribed position that the successful candidate maintains a current Working With Children Check which is satisfactory to the University. Please contact Recruitment@Flinders \u00a0by email at recruitment@flinders.edu.au \u00a0should you have any queries regarding Casual opportunities."}, "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Bedford-Park--Kaurna-Country/Casual-Academic-Register---Health-Sciences---Allied-Health_JR0000010261": {"title": "Casual Academic Register - Health Sciences & Allied Health", "description": "Posted: 2026-02-26\nPart time\n\nAbout Flinders Our bold ambition, articulated in our Strategic Plan Impact. With Purpose: The 2035 Agenda , is to change 10 million lives for the better by opening opportunities, solving real\u2011world problems, and translating knowledge into outcomes that strengthen communities. \u00a0 With a renewed focus on putting students first, being the university for industry and enterprise, and delivering research that creates meaningful impact, we recognise that exceptional people are central to our success. Casual Register About the College of Nursing and Health Sciences\u00a0 \u00a0 At the College of Nursing and Health Sciences, we aim to be an innovator in contemporary education producing a safer and more resilient health and social care workforce. Our mission is to improve lives and empower communities, enabling better health and caring in the world through an exceptional student learning experience. At the College, our research mission is about co-creating new knowledge which promotes wellbeing, and better care and support, to individuals and communities across the lifespan. We work proactively with industry partners and professional bodies leading to more employable and innovative graduates. \u00a0 Casual Register Opportunities \u00a0 Flinders University has several casual registers where people can express their interest in casual work, if and when opportunities become available. This particular register is for roles in Health Sciences and Allied Health. Work may be available in both undergraduate and postgraduate courses and could take place at our Bedford Park campus, one of our regional campuses (Riverland, Port Pirie, or Mount Gambier), or online from any location. \u00a0 Selection Criteria You are currently registered, or can be registered, as an Allied Health practitioner with AHPRA (if required for your role). You have, or can get, a valid South Australian Working with Children Check. Passionate about teaching and enjoy helping the next generation of graduates learn and grow in your field. Strong communication and teamwork skills. Knowledge and/or experience with current trends in health sciences and allied health. Experience teaching in a university setting (desirable). A postgraduate qualification in health or a related field (desirable). How to Register Upload your current CV/Resume detailing your qualifications and experience You may choose to upload a Cover Letter of no more than 1 page to support your CV/Resume Your application will be acknowledged by an automated e-mail once submitted. If a casual opportunity is available and your application is considered suitable, the relevant hiring manager will contact you for a further discussion. Please note, only suitable applicants will be contacted. Applying to the Casual Register does not guarantee employment. Further Information Pursuant to Child Safety (Prohibited Persons) Act 2016 (SA) this position may be deemed prescribed.\u00a0It is an inherent requirement of a prescribed position that the successful candidate maintains a current Working With Children Check which is satisfactory to the University Please contact recruitment@flinders.edu.au \u00a0should you have any queries regarding casual opportunities."}, "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Bedford-Park/Casual-Professional-Register---Learning-Advisor_JR0000000101": {"title": "Casual Professional Register - Learning Advisor", "description": "Posted: 2026-02-26\nPart time\n\nAbout Flinders Our bold ambition, articulated in our Strategic Plan Impact. With Purpose: The 2035 Agenda , is to change 10 million lives for the better by opening opportunities, solving real\u2011world problems, and translating knowledge into outcomes that strengthen communities. \u00a0 With a renewed focus on putting students first, being the university for industry and enterprise, and delivering research that creates meaningful impact, we recognise that exceptional people are central to our success. Casual Register Flinders University has a number of Casual Registers as a means of expressions of interest for the purpose of casual work, should such opportunities arise. We recognise the key to our success is exceptional people and we welcome registrations of interest from individuals wishing to join our team on a casual or short-term basis. How to Register: Upload your current CV/Resum\u00e9 detailing your qualifications and experience. You may choose to upload a Cover Letter of no more than 1 page to support your CV/Resum\u00e9. Your application will be acknowledged by an automated e-mail once submitted. If a casual opportunity is available and your application is considered suitable, the relevant hiring manager will contact you for a further discussion. Please note, only suitable applicants will be contacted. Applying to the Casual Register does not guarantee employment. Further Information: Pursuant to Child Safety (Prohibited Persons) Act 2016 (SA) this position may be deemed prescribed.\u00a0 It is an inherent requirement of a prescribed position that the successful candidate maintains a current Working With Children Check which is satisfactory to the University. Please contact Recruitment@Flinders \u00a0by email at recruitment@flinders.edu.au \u00a0should you have any queries regarding Casual opportunities."}, "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Bedford-Park/Casual-Professional-Register---Flinders-Connect_JR0000000100": {"title": "Casual Professional Register \u2013 Flinders Connect", "description": "Posted: 2026-02-26\nPart time\n\nAbout Flinders Our bold ambition, articulated in our Strategic Plan Impact. With Purpose: The 2035 Agenda , is to change 10 million lives for the better by opening opportunities, solving real\u2011world problems, and translating knowledge into outcomes that strengthen communities. \u00a0 With a renewed focus on putting students first, being the university for industry and enterprise, and delivering research that creates meaningful impact, we recognise that exceptional people are central to our success. Casual Register Flinders Connect offers in-person, phone and online support for student related issues such as enrolment, fees, exams, graduations, and general queries.\u00a0 We recognise the key to our success is exceptional people and we welcome registrations of interest from individuals wishing to join our team on a casual or short-term basis. How to Register: Upload your current CV/Resum\u00e9 detailing your qualifications and experience. You may choose to upload a Cover Letter of no more than 1 page to support your CV/Resum\u00e9. Your application will be acknowledged by an automated e-mail once submitted. If a casual opportunity is available and your application is considered suitable, the relevant hiring manager will contact you for a further discussion. Please note, only suitable applicants will be contacted. Applying to the Casual Register does not guarantee employment. Further Information: Pursuant to Child Safety (Prohibited Persons) Act 2016 (SA) this position may be deemed prescribed.\u00a0 It is an inherent requirement of a prescribed position that the successful candidate maintains a current Working With Children Check which is satisfactory to the University. Please contact Recruitment@Flinders \u00a0by email at recruitment@flinders.edu.au \u00a0should you have any queries regarding Casual opportunities."}, "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Bedford-Park/Casual-Professional-Register---Technical-Support---Research_JR0000000098-1": {"title": "Casual Professional Register - Technical Support / Research", "description": "Posted: 2026-02-26\nPart time\n\nAbout Flinders Our bold ambition, articulated in our Strategic Plan Impact. With Purpose: The 2035 Agenda , is to change 10 million lives for the better by opening opportunities, solving real\u2011world problems, and translating knowledge into outcomes that strengthen communities. \u00a0 With a renewed focus on putting students first, being the university for industry and enterprise, and delivering research that creates meaningful impact, we recognise that exceptional people are central to our success. Casual Register Flinders University has a number of Casual Registers as a means of expressions of interest for the purpose of casual work, should such opportunities arise. How to Register: Upload your current CV/Resum\u00e9 detailing your qualifications and experience. You may choose to upload a Cover Letter of no more than 1 page to support your CV/Resum\u00e9. Your application will be acknowledged by an automated e-mail once submitted. If a casual opportunity is available and your application is considered suitable, the relevant hiring manager will contact you for a further discussion. Please note, only suitable applicants will be contacted. Applying to the Casual Register does not guarantee employment. Further Information: Pursuant to Child Safety (Prohibited Persons) Act 2016 (SA) this position may be deemed prescribed.\u00a0 It is an inherent requirement of a prescribed position that the successful candidate maintains a current Working With Children Check which is satisfactory to the University. Please contact Recruitment@Flinders \u00a0by email at recruitment@flinders.edu.au \u00a0should you have any queries regarding Casual opportunities."}, "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Bedford-Park/Casual-Professional-Register---Library-Officer---Librarian-or-Library-Assistant_JR0000000097": {"title": "Casual Professional Register - Library Officer / Librarian or Library Assistant", "description": "Posted: 2026-02-26\nPart time\n\nAbout Flinders Our bold ambition, articulated in our Strategic Plan Impact. With Purpose: The 2035 Agenda , is to change 10 million lives for the better by opening opportunities, solving real\u2011world problems, and translating knowledge into outcomes that strengthen communities. \u00a0 With a renewed focus on putting students first, being the university for industry and enterprise, and delivering research that creates meaningful impact, we recognise that exceptional people are central to our success. Casual Register Flinders University has a number of Casual Registers as a means of expressions of interest for the purpose of casual work, should such opportunities arise. We recognise the key to our success is exceptional people and we welcome registrations of interest from current Flinders students wishing to join our team on a casual or short-term basis. To Register: Upload your current CV/Resum\u00e9 detailing your qualifications and experience. You may choose to upload a Cover Letter of no more than 1 page to support your CV/Resum\u00e9. Your application will be acknowledged by an automated e-mail once submitted. If a casual opportunity is available and your application is considered suitable, the relevant hiring manager will contact you for a further discussion. Please note, these registers are consulted only when an opportunity arises, and only suitable applicants will be contacted. Applying to the Casual Register does not guarantee employment. To be eligible for casual opportunities, you must have the right to work in Australia. A current Nationally Coordinated Criminal History Check which is satisfactory to the University will be required by Flinders University before the successful applicant can commence in this position. A criminal record will not automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration. Each case will be assessed on its individual merits and relevance to the inherent requirements of the role. Pursuant to Child Safety (Prohibited Persons) Act 2016 (SA) this position may be deemed prescribed.\u00a0 It is an inherent requirement of a prescribed position that the successful candidate maintains a current Working With Children Check which is satisfactory to the University. Please contact the recruitment team\u00a0by email at talent.aquistion@flinders.edu.au\u00a0should you have any queries regarding Casual opportunities."}, "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Bedford-Park/Casual-Professional-Register---Information-Technology_JR0000000096": {"title": "Casual Professional Register - Information Technology", "description": "Posted: 2026-02-26\nPart time\n\nAbout Flinders Our bold ambition, articulated in our Strategic Plan Impact. With Purpose: The 2035 Agenda , is to change 10 million lives for the better by opening opportunities, solving real\u2011world problems, and translating knowledge into outcomes that strengthen communities. \u00a0 With a renewed focus on putting students first, being the university for industry and enterprise, and delivering research that creates meaningful impact, we recognise that exceptional people are central to our success. Casual Register Flinders University has a number of Casual Registers as a means of expressions of interest for the purpose of casual work, should such opportunities arise. We recognise the key to our success is exceptional people and we welcome registrations of interest from individuals wishing to join our team on a casual or short-term basis. To Register: Upload your current CV/Resum\u00e9 detailing your qualifications and experience. You may choose to upload a Cover Letter of no more than 1 page to support your CV/Resum\u00e9. Your application will be acknowledged by an automated e-mail once submitted. If a casual opportunity is available and your application is considered suitable, the relevant hiring manager will contact you for a further discussion. Please note, these registers are consulted only when an opportunity arises, and only suitable applicants will be contacted. Applying to the Casual Register does not guarantee employment. To be eligible for casual opportunities, you must have the right to work in Australia. A current Nationally Coordinated Criminal History Check which is satisfactory to the University may be required by Flinders University before a successful applicant can commence in this position. A criminal record will not automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration. Each case will be assessed on its individual merits and relevance to the inherent requirements of the role. Pursuant to Child Safety (Prohibited Persons) Act 2016 (SA) this position may be deemed prescribed.\u00a0 It is an inherent requirement of a prescribed position that the successful candidate maintains a current Working With Children Check which is satisfactory to the University. Please contact the recruitment team\u00a0by email at talent.aquistion@flinders.edu.au\u00a0should you have any queries regarding Casual opportunities."}, "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Bedford-Park/Casual-Professional-Register---Administration-Finance_JR0000000095": {"title": "Casual Professional Register - Administration/Finance", "description": "Posted: 2026-02-26\nPart time\n\nAbout Flinders Our bold ambition, articulated in our Strategic Plan Impact. With Purpose: The 2035 Agenda , is to change 10 million lives for the better by opening opportunities, solving real\u2011world problems, and translating knowledge into outcomes that strengthen communities. \u00a0 With a renewed focus on putting students first, being the university for industry and enterprise, and delivering research that creates meaningful impact, we recognise that exceptional people are central to our success. Casual Register Flinders University has a number of Casual Registers as a means of expressions of interest for the purpose of casual work, should such opportunities arise . \u00a0 We recognise the key to our success is exceptional people and we welcome registrations of interest from individuals wishing to join our team on a casual or short-term basis. \u00a0 To Register: \u00a0 Upload your current CV/Resum\u00e9 detailing your qualifications and experience. \u00a0 You may choose to upload a Cover Letter of no more than 1 page to support your CV/Resum\u00e9. \u00a0 Your application will be acknowledged by an automated e-mail once submitted . \u00a0 If a casual opportunity is available and your application is considered suitable, the relevant hiring manager will contact you for a further discussion. \u00a0 Please note, these registers are consulted only \u00a0 when an opportunity arises, and only suitable applicants will be contacted. Applying to the Casual Register does not guarantee employment. \u00a0 To be eligible for casual opportunities, you must have the right to work in Australia . \u00a0 A current Nationally Coordinated Criminal History Check which is satisfactory to the University may be required by Flinders University before a successful applicant can commence in this position. A criminal record will not automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration. Each case will be assessed on its individual merits and relevance to the inherent requirements of the role. \u00a0 Pursuant to Child Safety (Prohibited Persons) Act 2016 (SA) this position may be deemed prescribed.\u202f It is an inherent requirement of a prescribed position that the successful candidate maintains a current Working With Children Check which is satisfactory to the University. \u00a0 Please contact the recruitment team\u202fby email at talent.aquistion@flinders.edu.au\u202f should you have any queries regarding Casual opportunities."}, "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Bedford-Park/Casual-Academic-Register---Placement-Facilitator--CNHS-_JR0000000094": {"title": "Casual Academic Register \u2013 Placement Facilitator (CNHS)", "description": "Posted: 2026-02-26\nPart time\n\nAbout Flinders Our bold ambition, articulated in our Strategic Plan Impact. With Purpose: The 2035 Agenda , is to change 10 million lives for the better by opening opportunities, solving real\u2011world problems, and translating knowledge into outcomes that strengthen communities. \u00a0 With a renewed focus on putting students first, being the university for industry and enterprise, and delivering research that creates meaningful impact, we recognise that exceptional people are central to our success. Casual Register The College of Nursing and Health Sciences is currently seeking expressions of interest from suitably qualified individuals who would be available to undertake casual Placement Educator (Facilitation) opportunities to support Nursing undergraduate and postgraduate student learning during their professional placement experiences across a range of health care settings. Casual Placement Educator (Facilitation) staff will report to the Topic Coordinators and be responsible for: establishing and maintaining professional relationships with venues and the clinical teams to support student learning through aspects such as (but not limited to) advocating for appropriate learning experiences, allocation of students to shifts, clarifying students scope of practice, allocation of preceptors, navigating issues or concerns, seeking feedback on student progress regular and timely communication with Topic Coordinators and students in relation to student progress and identified concerns attending pre-clinical meetings for allocated students meeting with each student for 2.5 hours each week (30 minutes/day) to discuss progress and facilitate learning through reflection on experiences, supporting links between theory and practice to foster meaning making understanding students\u2019 scope of practice, expected learning outcomes of the topic and how this applies to student practice as reflected in the Placement Assessment Record providing ongoing constructive feedback to students to optimise their learning outcomes recording each student meeting, identifying progress, content of discussion and plan for development developing Professional Learning Plans collaboratively with students and Topic Coordinators that supports student learning mentoring professional standards, attitudes and attributes of the Registered Nurse completing assessment requirements for individual students (Placement Assessment Records, Viva voce, attendance records etc) SELECTION CRITERIA Holds an Australian Bachelor of Nursing Degree or higher qualification. Currently registered with the Australian Health Practitioner Regulation Agency (AHPRA). Current or eligible to register for a Working with Children Check from the Department of Human Services \u2013 SA Government (or equivalent State or Territory requirement). A minimum of three years full-time clinical experience. Experience of teaching and learning in your role as a Registered Nurse. Demonstrated excellent interpersonal, collaborative and communication skills. Demonstrated problem solving, conflict resolution and negotiation skills. Demonstrated knowledge and/or experience in using technology such as Microsoft Office programs and interactive online technology. A willingness to travel between clinical venues. Evidence of employment in a clinical education role (desirable) Holding a Graduate Diploma, Masters or PhD in nursing or related field (desirable). HOW TO APPLY AND GENERAL INFORMATION Click on Apply and submit a completed CV/R\u00e9sum\u00e9 and Cover Letter of no more than two-pages that also addresses the selection criteria; dot point statements can be used. You will also need to complete the online registration form and include your AHPRA registration number and Working with Children Check details. All information submitted is stored securely within our database, accessible only to senior staff members of the teaching sections of Nursing. If successful, your details will be added to the Casual register. The register is used by Topic Coordinators to identify potential staff and they will contact you about placement educator opportunities. If you have not received communication regarding your application within 4 weeks, please be advised that your application will not progress further at this time. Please contact nhsenquiries@flinders.edu.au should you have any queries regarding Casual PEP Facilitator Opportunities in the College of Nursing and Health Sciences. Please note: Pursuant to Child Safety (Prohibited Persons) Act 2016 (SA) this position has been deemed prescribed.\u00a0 It is an inherent requirement of the position that the successful candidate maintains a current Working With Children Check which is satisfactory to the University. A valid National Police Certificate which is satisfactory to the University will also be required before the successful applicant can commence in this position."}, "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Bedford-Park/Casual-Academic-Register---College-of-Medicine-and-Public-Health_JR0000000092": {"title": "Casual Academic Register \u2013 College of Medicine and Public Health", "description": "Posted: 2026-02-26\nPart time\n\nAbout Flinders Our bold ambition, articulated in our Strategic Plan Impact. With Purpose: The 2035 Agenda , is to change 10 million lives for the better by opening opportunities, solving real\u2011world problems, and translating knowledge into outcomes that strengthen communities. \u00a0 With a renewed focus on putting students first, being the university for industry and enterprise, and delivering research that creates meaningful impact, we recognise that exceptional people are central to our success. Casual Register Flinders University has a number of Casual Registers as a means of expressions of interest for the purpose of casual work, should such opportunities arise. How to Register: Upload your current CV/Resum\u00e9 detailing your qualifications and experience. You may choose to upload a Cover Letter of no more than 1 page to support your CV/Resum\u00e9. Your application will be acknowledged by an automated e-mail once submitted. If a casual opportunity is available and your application is considered suitable, the relevant hiring manager will contact you for a further discussion. Please note, only suitable applicants will be contacted. Applying to the Casual Register does not guarantee employment. Further Information: Pursuant to Child Safety (Prohibited Persons) Act 2016 (SA) this position may be deemed prescribed.\u00a0 It is an inherent requirement of a prescribed position that the successful candidate maintains a current Working With Children Check which is satisfactory to the University. Please contact Recruitment@Flinders \u00a0by email at recruitment@flinders.edu.au \u00a0should you have any queries regarding Casual opportunities."}, "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Bedford-Park/Casual-Academic-Register---College-of-Nursing-and-Health-Sciences_JR0000000089": {"title": "Casual Academic Register \u2013 College of Nursing and Health Sciences", "description": "Posted: 2026-02-26\nPart time\n\nAbout Flinders Our bold ambition, articulated in our Strategic Plan Impact. With Purpose: The 2035 Agenda , is to change 10 million lives for the better by opening opportunities, solving real\u2011world problems, and translating knowledge into outcomes that strengthen communities. \u00a0 With a renewed focus on putting students first, being the university for industry and enterprise, and delivering research that creates meaningful impact, we recognise that exceptional people are central to our success. Casual Register About the College of Nursing and Health Sciences\u00a0 \u00a0 At the College of Nursing and Health Sciences, we aim to be an innovator in contemporary education producing a safer and more resilient health and social care workforce. Our mission is to improve lives and empower communities, enabling better health and caring in the world through an exceptional student learning experience. At the College, our research mission is about co-creating new knowledge which promotes wellbeing, and better care and support, to individuals and communities across the lifespan. We work proactively with industry partners and professional bodies leading to more employable and innovative graduates. \u00a0 Casual Register Opportunities \u00a0 Flinders University has several casual registers where people can express their interest in casual work, if and when opportunities become available. This particular register is for roles in Health Sciences and Allied Health. Work may be available in both undergraduate and postgraduate courses and could take place at our Bedford Park campus, one of our regional campuses (Riverland, Port Pirie, or Mount Gambier), or online from any location. \u00a0 Selection Criteria You are currently registered, or can be registered, as an Allied Health practitioner with AHPRA (if required for your role). You have, or can get, a valid South Australian Working with Children Check. Passionate about teaching and enjoy helping the next generation of graduates learn and grow in your field. Strong communication and teamwork skills. Knowledge and/or experience with current trends in health sciences and allied health. Experience teaching in a university setting (desirable). A postgraduate qualification in health or a related field (desirable). How to Register Upload your current CV/Resume detailing your qualifications and experience You may choose to upload a Cover Letter of no more than 1 page to support your CV/Resume Your application will be acknowledged by an automated e-mail once submitted. If a casual opportunity is available and your application is considered suitable, the relevant hiring manager will contact you for a further discussion. Please note, only suitable applicants will be contacted. Applying to the Casual Register does not guarantee employment. Further Information Pursuant to Child Safety (Prohibited Persons) Act 2016 (SA) this position may be deemed prescribed.\u00a0It is an inherent requirement of a prescribed position that the successful candidate maintains a current Working With Children Check which is satisfactory to the University Please contact recruitment@flinders.edu.au \u00a0should you have any queries regarding casual opportunities."}, "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Bedford-Park/Casual-Academic-Register---College-of-Science-and-Engineering_JR0000000088": {"title": "Casual Academic Register \u2013 College of Science and Engineering", "description": "Posted: 2026-02-26\nPart time\n\nAbout Flinders Our bold ambition, articulated in our Strategic Plan Impact. With Purpose: The 2035 Agenda , is to change 10 million lives for the better by opening opportunities, solving real\u2011world problems, and translating knowledge into outcomes that strengthen communities. \u00a0 With a renewed focus on putting students first, being the university for industry and enterprise, and delivering research that creates meaningful impact, we recognise that exceptional people are central to our success. Casual Register Flinders University has a number of Casual Registers as a means of expressions of interest for the purpose of casual work, should such opportunities arise. How to Register: Upload your current CV/Resum\u00e9 detailing your qualifications and experience. You may choose to upload a Cover Letter of no more than 1 page to support your CV/Resum\u00e9. Your application will be acknowledged by an automated e-mail once submitted. If a casual opportunity is available and your application is considered suitable, the relevant hiring manager will contact you for a further discussion. Please note, only suitable applicants will be contacted. Applying to the Casual Register does not guarantee employment. Further Information: Pursuant to Child Safety (Prohibited Persons) Act 2016 (SA) this position may be deemed prescribed.\u00a0 It is an inherent requirement of a prescribed position that the successful candidate maintains a current Working With Children Check which is satisfactory to the University. Please contact Recruitment@Flinders \u00a0by email at recruitment@flinders.edu.au \u00a0should you have any queries regarding Casual opportunities."}, "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Bedford-Park/Casual-Academic-Register---College-of-Humanities--Arts-and-Social-Sciences_JR0000000090": {"title": "Casual Academic Register \u2013 College of Humanities, Arts and Social Sciences", "description": "Posted: 2024-11-18\nPart time\n\nAbout Flinders Our bold vision, captured in our Strategic Plan: Making a Difference: The 2025 Agenda, is to be internationally recognised as a world leader in research, an innovator in contemporary education, and the source of Australia\u2019s most enterprising graduates. To realise this ambition, we recently made a significant organisational change to a six College structure with a professional staff and services alignment. We recognise the key to our success is exceptional people and we\u2019re seeking an outstanding individual to join the leadership team of our transformed university. Casual Register Flinders University has a number of Casual Registers as a means of expressions of interest for the purpose of casual work, should such opportunities arise. How to Register: Upload your current CV/Resum\u00e9 detailing your qualifications and experience. You may choose to upload a Cover Letter of no more than 1 page to support your CV/Resum\u00e9. Your application will be acknowledged by an automated e-mail once submitted. If a casual opportunity is available and your application is considered suitable, the relevant hiring manager will contact you for a further discussion. Please note, only suitable applicants will be contacted. Applying to the Casual Register does not guarantee employment. Further Information: Pursuant to Child Safety (Prohibited Persons) Act 2016 (SA) this position may be deemed prescribed.\u00a0 It is an inherent requirement of a prescribed position that the successful candidate maintains a current Working With Children Check which is satisfactory to the University. Please contact Recruitment@Flinders \u00a0by email at recruitment@flinders.edu.au \u00a0should you have any queries regarding Casual opportunities."}, "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Tonsley/Cisco-Research-Chair-in-Defence-Capability-and-Security_JR0000017614": {"title": "Cisco Research Chair in Defence Capability and Security", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-22\nFull time\n\nPosition Details Full Time | Five-year contract Academic Level E | AU$217,876 | 17% Superannuation Location: Tonsley / Kaurna Country /Australia View Position Description View Candidate Brochure A Position with Impact: Flinders University is at the frontline of defence-oriented research and is seeking an inaugural Cisco Research Chair in Defence Capability and Security. Based in Adelaide, Australia\u2019s Defence State, and home to some of the nation\u2019s most significant defence projects, investment and sovereign capability development, this is a nationally significant opportunity to lead research at the intersection of digital technology, defence and sovereign capability. With direct access to Cisco\u2019s technology and global research network, you will be positioned at the centre of an environment where Defence, industry, technology and government are actively shaping Australia\u2019s future capability. \u00a0 Working in partnership with Cisco, the Australian Defence Force, the Department of Defence and Australia\u2019s sovereign defence industry, you will establish and lead an applied research programme that translates emerging technologies into real-world defence capability. You will have the opportunity to shape research that advances AUKUS priorities, strengthens critical infrastructure resilience and builds Australia\u2019s sovereign defence capability. \u00a0 In this position, you will: Lead with impact: Establish and shape a high-profile applied research programme spanning AI, autonomous systems, advanced manufacturing and/or cyber security, translating emerging technology into capability for Defence and industry. Work at the forefront of innovation: Partner directly with Cisco, the Australian Defence Force, the Department of Defence and sovereign defence industry, with access to Cisco\u2019s next-generation networking, security, AI and IoT technologies and global research network. Build what comes next: Grow a team of researchers and HDR candidates, attract major research and industry investment, influence national conversations and help develop the sovereign technology capability Australia needs for the future. \u00a0 This is a flagship academic appointment established under the Flinders-Cisco partnership to advance defence capabilities through world-leading research innovation and impact. \u00a0 \u00a0 About You: You are an established researcher, technology leader or senior defence practitioner with a strong track record in defence, national security or digital technology. \u00a0 You will bring: A doctoral qualification in a relevant discipline OR equivalent achievement at a senior practitioner level in defence industries or national security Demonstrated expertise in advanced manufacturing, AI, autonomous systems (maritime) or cyber security for defence. A strong record of research, industry or government-funded programmes and/or competitive funding. The ability to translate technical innovation into real-world capability outcomes. Established networks across Defence, government, industry and/or the broader technology ecosystem. Exceptional communication and leadership skills, with the credibility to engage across technical, Defence, industry and policy environments. \u00a0 International and domestic candidates are welcome to apply. Eligibility and willingness to obtain an Australian Government security clearance at Negative Vetting Level 1 or higher is highly desirable. \u00a0 A Partnership Built for Innovation: Flinders University and Cisco have established one of Australia\u2019s leading university-industry partnerships in digital innovation and applied research. Since 2015, the partnership has evolved into an integrated ecosystem spanning world-class research, industry collaboration, student innovation, workforce development and translational impact. Through a complementary national network of Cisco Chairs, Innovation Central Adelaide, and the National Industry Innovation Network (NIIN), the partnership provides a nationally connected innovation ecosystem that accelerates research impact and translation, industry collaboration, talent development and the adoption of new technologies to address complex industry challenges. As the Cisco Research Chair, you will be embedded within this dynamic ecosystem, connecting world-class research with Cisco technology, industry expertise and real-world opportunities to deliver impact in Australia and beyond. Why Flinders University? They say know your place.\u00a0 We say you've found it right here. \u00a0 Flinders University was founded on the belief that learning should open minds, celebrate individuality and give people the freedom to pursue their own point of view. That spirit lives on in our community of thinkers, doers and changemakers who challenge convention, and each other, to shape what comes next. \u00a0 Rising to a challenge is nothing new for Flinders. During our first 60 years, we\u2019ve navigated revolutionary changes in social and cultural norms, and have responded to transformative economic, environmental and technological developments. Through it all, we\u2019ve continued to deliver for our students and community, innovating in learning and research to prepare graduates for the changing world they help create. \u00a0 Reaching beyond the limits of buildings, borders, and backgrounds, ours is an inclusive culture that believes absolutely in equality and opportunity for all. We don't just accommodate differences; we embrace and celebrate them. \u00a0 So,\u00a0 why work at Flinders? Recognised as the top 2% university worldwide, with research income soaring to $133 million in research contracts and grants. 17% Superannuation + salary packaging options Flexible working arrangements Awarded the AHEIA Higher Education Award for Workplace Culture Excellence due to our commitment to wellbeing through our\u00a0 Thriving@Flinders \u00a0staff wellbeing program Wide range of professional development activities and services, including exclusive staff study offers\u00a0 We embrace diversity and promote equity and inclusion for all students and staff, as shown through our three SAGE Cygnet Awards. Vibrant campus life and amenities including on campus\u00a0 health care services ,\u00a0 gym \u00a0and\u00a0 childcare centre (Bedford Park, South Australia Recognised as a Veteran Employer of Choice\u00a0 \u00a0 Our Commitment to Reconciliation and Indigenous Employment Flinders University is proud to be an organisation that is committed to our Reconciliation Action Plan and Indigenous Workforce Strategy. Our vision is to be a preferred employer for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples. We are committed to progressing Indigenous advancement in education, research, employment, and wellbeing, and strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all Flinders vacancies. Prescribed Conditions for Employment Appointment to this role is conditional on the completion of required pre\u2011employment checks and declarations, each of which must be satisfactory to the University. This includes a Gender\u2011Based Violence declaration, in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender\u2011Based Violence (2025), and a Nationally Coordinated Criminal History Check. An NCCHC disclosable outcome\u00a0will not automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration. Each case will be assessed on its individual merits and relevance to the inherent requirements of the role.\u00a0 How to Apply and Information You are required to submit a CV and a three-page Suitability Statement addressing the key position capabilities of the position description . For more information regarding this position, we strongly encourage you to please conta ct Professor Michael Blumenstein via Cse.operations@flinders.edu.au . Applications to be submitted before 10:00 pm (ACDT) on Wednesday, 21 October 2026. Please note, late applications and applications sent via agencies will not be accepted . At Flinders we embrace and celebrate diversity and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people of all ages, ethnicities, abilities, sexual orientations, and gender identities. Certification Applications to be submitted before 10.00pm: 21 Oct 2026 At Flinders we embrace and celebrate diversity and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people of all ages, ethnicities, abilities, sexual orientations, and gender identities. Flinders. Fearless."}, "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Centre-for-Remote-Health-Alice-Springs/Lecturer-in-Remote-Health--Nursing-_JR0000017148": {"title": "Lecturer in Remote Health (Nursing)", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-25\nFull time\n\nPosition Details Fixed Term until 31 December 2027 | Up to full-time hours available (0.6 to 1.0 FTE negotiable) Academic Level B | $115,871 - $137,122 p.a. Location: Alice Springs - Arrernte View Position Description About the Role Join our Rural and Remote Health team as a Lecturer in Remote Health (Nursing), where you will play a key role in preparing and supporting the future health workforce for remote and Indigenous communities. This teaching-focused position contributes to excellence in nursing and remote health education through innovative, student-centred learning experiences. Working within a multidisciplinary team across the Northern Territory, you will deliver high-quality teaching, develop contemporary curriculum, and help equip graduates with the skills and knowledge required to thrive in remote acute and primary healthcare settings. Key responsibilities include: Delivering engaging and innovative teaching across nursing and remote health topics, using contemporary educational practices and technologies to enhance student success. Developing, coordinating and reviewing curriculum and learning materials, including undertaking Topic Coordinator responsibilities as required. Providing academic guidance, mentoring and professional advice to support students' learning, career development and readiness for practice. Building and maintaining strong partnerships with healthcare providers, professional bodies and communities to enhance student learning opportunities and workforce outcomes in rural and remote health. \u00a0 This position makes a significant contribution to the University\u2019s strategic plan to change 10 million lives, Every One Matters, by 2035, through directly contributing to the strategic driver of Student Centricity. By delivering innovative, high-quality nursing and remote health education, supporting student success, and preparing graduates for impactful careers in remote and Indigenous healthcare settings, the role helps create meaningful outcomes for students, communities and the health workforce. \u00a0 About You You are a passionate and experienced nursing educator with a commitment to student success and excellence in teaching. Bringing contemporary professional expertise and strong tertiary teaching capability, you thrive in collaborative environments and are motivated by the opportunity to prepare the next generation of health professionals for practice in rural, remote and Indigenous healthcare settings. You combine innovative teaching approaches with outstanding communication and relationship-building skills to create engaging and supportive learning experiences. You have a strong track record of designing and delivering innovative, student-centred learning experiences, including the effective use of online and educational technologies. You possess excellent interpersonal, written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to build effective relationships with students, colleagues, industry partners and community stakeholders. You bring experience in curriculum development, academic quality processes and coordinating teaching activities, alongside an ongoing commitment to professional engagement and continuous improvement. \u00a0 Flinders Rural and Remote Health NT At Flinders Rural and Remote Health NT , our aim is to be a hub for innovative health research, education, and workforce development across the Northern Territory.\u00a0 We engage with students, community, and stakeholders to provide critical programs, such as the Northern Territory Medical Program, Paramedicine, Rural Clinical School, and the University Department of Rural Health. Our postgraduate education pathways (Remote Health Practice program), provides workforce development through Indigenous health and clinical skills training, and we have a community driven research program led by researchers committed to improving health outcomes. We work alongside Poche SA+NT focussing on Indigenous leadership capacity development and developing the Indigenous health workforce.\u00a0 All activities are driven by our values which focus on the long-term and short-term needs of the NT community. Life at Flinders We're transforming and investing in people and facilities to create contemporary, stimulating, and satisfying learning and work environments that reflect our core values of excellence, innovation, courage, and integrity. Flinders is refocusing its strategic priorities with the aim of elevating its performance to be a top ten Australian university, and amongst the top 1% in the world. Reaching beyond the limits of buildings, borders, and backgrounds, ours is an inclusive culture that believes absolutely in equality and opportunity for all. We don't just accommodate differences; we embrace and celebrate them. So,\u00a0 why work at Flinders? 17% Superannuation + salary packaging options Flexible working arrangements Awarded the AHEIA Higher Education Award for Workplace Culture Excellence due to our commitment to wellbeing through our Thriving@Flinders staff wellbeing program Wide range of professional development activities and services, including exclusive staff study offers\u00a0 We embrace diversity and promote equity and inclusion for all students and staff, as shown through our three SAGE Cygnet Awards. Recognised as a Veteran Employer of Choice 6 weeks annual leave (Northern Territory)\u00a0 Our Commitment to Reconciliation and Indigenous Employment Flinders University is proud to be an organisation that is committed to our Reconciliation Action Plan and Indigenous Workforce Strategy. Our vision is to be a preferred employer for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples.\u00a0 We are committed to progressing Indigenous advancement in education, research, employment, and wellbeing, and strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all Flinders vacancies. \u00a0 Please see here for our Reconciliation Action Plan \u00a0 Please see here for our Indigenous Workforce Strategy \u00a0 Prescribed Conditions for Employment A current Nationally Coordinated Criminal History Check which is satisfactory to the University will be required by Flinders University before the successful applicant can commence in this position. A criminal record will not automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration. Each case will be assessed on its individual merits and relevance to the inherent requirements of the role. Please note that you may be required to provide evidence that you are up to date with COVID-19 vaccinations, in line with the Flinders University\u202f COVID-19 Vaccination Policy \u00a0 Northern Territory Government legislation (the Care and Protection of Children Act 2007) now requires all individuals in child related employment or whose duties involve, or are likely to involve, contact with a child, to hold a valid 'Working with Children Clearance' (Ochre Card). This position involves child related work and is assessed as requiring a Working with Children Clearance/Ochre Card. A valid Northern Territory (NT) Driver\u2019s License is an essential requirement of this position and must be maintained for the duration of employment. How to Apply and Information You are required to submit a CV, along with a Suitability Statement as a separate document.\u00a0 This should be no more than 3 pages, and address the Key Position Capabilities of the position description . Flinders University is committed to providing an environment where staff with disability are valued, supported and encouraged, and can, as far as practicably possible, participate fully and independently in the life of the University.\u00a0If you require any reasonable adjustments to assist you in the selection process, including being accompanied by an accredited assistance animal with public access rights as per the Disability Policy , please advise the contact the Recruitment Team so that we can make appropriate arrangements through recruitment@flinders.edu.au or call 08 8201 2383. For more information regarding this position, please contact Kim Pearce Applications to be submitted before 10:00 pm (ACDT) Sunday, 25 October 2026. Please note, late applications and applications sent via agencies will not be accepted . At Flinders we embrace and celebrate diversity and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people of all ages, ethnicities, abilities, sexual orientations, and gender identities. Certification Applications to be submitted before 10.00pm: 25 Oct 2026 At Flinders we embrace and celebrate diversity and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people of all ages, ethnicities, abilities, sexual orientations, and gender identities. Flinders. Fearless."}, "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Bedford-Park--Kaurna-Country/Senior-Lecturer-Lecturer-in-Midwifery_JR0000017694": {"title": "Senior Lecturer/Lecturer in Midwifery", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-01\nFull time\n\nPosition Details Continuing | Full-Time or Part-Time available Academic Level B or C | $115,871 - $162,619 p.a. pro-rata Location: Bedford Park / Kaurna Country View Position Description \u2013 Lecturer Teaching Specialist (Clinical Practitioner) View Position Description \u2013 Senior Lecturer Teaching Specialist (Clinical Practitioner) About the Role/s Lecturer The Lecturer in Midwifery - Teaching Specialist (Clinical Practitioner), will contribute to excellence in teaching and learning across a range of midwifery topics. The lecturer will play a key role in developing and delivering high-quality, innovative teaching through lectures, tutorials, clinical placements, and contemporary digital strategies. This includes creating course materials, coordinating placements, and conducting assessments. The role also requires ongoing clinical or community-based practice to maintain current skills and knowledge. In addition, the incumbent will provide informal leadership by supporting academic staff, coordinating workflows, and ensuring high standards aligned with university policies and practices. Senior Lecturer The Senior Lecturer in Midwifery \u2013 Teaching Specialist (Clinical Practitioner), will provide leadership in delivering excellence in teaching and learning across the suite of Midwifery topics and courses in the College of Healthcare and Enablement, that enhance the student experience. The role will provide educational leadership; curriculum design and review; delivery innovation; advancements in education technologies; and leadership in ensuring internal and external compliance and accreditation of courses and continuous quality improvement of university-level education. The Senior Lecturer will also be expected to concurrently engage in practice in a clinical or community setting to support maintenance of contemporary practice, knowledge and skills. Please refer to the attached position descriptions for a comprehensive list of roles and responsibilities. This position makes a significant contribution to the University\u2019s strategic plan to changing 10 million lives, Every One Matters, by 2035 through a commitment to a student-centred ethos and to developing creative, enterprising, career-ready graduates prepared to become lifelong contributors to society. \u00a0 About You The Lecturer will have demonstrated excellence in tertiary teaching across classroom, simulation and/or clinical settings, including placement coordination. You will have a proven ability to independently contribute to the development, delivery and evaluation of innovative teaching and learning strategies, including student assessment, and an understanding of the nexus between teaching and learning, research, scholarship and practice. Additionally, as the Senior Lecturer, you will have significant and sustained evidence of excellence in tertiary teaching, including experience in simulation and/or clinical settings. You will have a strong track record of developing, delivering and evaluating innovative teaching and learning strategies across classroom and clinical education environments, together with a demonstrated commitment to teaching scholarship and professional development in higher education. You will have a strong understanding of the nexus between teaching and learning, research, scholarship and practice, together with experience coordinating and/or leading the teaching activities of colleagues. In these roles you will also be able to demonstrate: \u00a0 A completion of a PhD, or other relevant and equivalent qualification and/or experience. Hold and maintain a current membership with Nursing and Midwifery Board of Australia & Australian Health Practitioner Regulation Agency (AHPRA). Relevant and contemporary clinical experience as an accredited Midwife. An understanding of pedagogical theory and contemporary educational practice relevant to Midwifery. Excellent oral and written communication skills and interpersonal skills, including the demonstrated ability to establish effective relationships with staff, students and industry. \u00a0 \u00a0 College of Health and Enablement\u00a0 \u00a0 At the College of Health and Enablement, we aim to be an innovator in contemporary education producing a safer and more resilient health and social care workforce. Our mission is to improve lives and empower communities, enabling better health and caring in the world through an exceptional student learning experience. At the College, our research mission is about co-creating new knowledge which promotes wellbeing, and better care and support, to individuals and communities across the lifespan. We work proactively with industry partners and professional bodies leading to more employable and innovative graduates.\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 Life at Flinders \u00a0 They say know your place.\u00a0 We say you've found it right here. Flinders University was founded on the belief that learning should open minds, celebrate individuality and give people the freedom to pursue their own point of view. That spirit lives on in our community of thinkers, doers and changemakers who challenge convention, and each other, to shape what comes next. Rising to a challenge is nothing new for Flinders. During our first 60 years, we\u2019ve navigated revolutionary changes in social and cultural norms, and have responded to transformative economic, environmental and technological developments. Through it all, we\u2019ve continued to deliver for our students and community, innovating in learning and research to prepare graduates for the changing world they help create. Reaching beyond the limits of buildings, borders, and backgrounds, ours is an inclusive culture that believes absolutely in equality and opportunity for all. We don't just accommodate differences; we embrace and celebrate them. So, \u00a0 why work at Flinders? \u00a0 17% Superannuation + salary packaging options Flexible working arrangements Awarded the AHEIA Higher Education Award for Workplace Culture Excellence due to our commitment to wellbeing through our Thriving@Flinders staff wellbeing program Wide range of professional development activities and services, including exclusive staff study offers\u00a0 We embrace diversity and promote equity and inclusion for all students and staff, as shown through our three SAGE Cygnet Awards. Vibrant campus life and amenities including on campus\u00a0 health care services ,\u00a0 gym \u00a0and\u00a0 childcare centre (Bedford Park, South Australia). Recognised as a Veteran Employer of Choice\u00a0 \u00a0 Our Commitment to Reconciliation and Indigenous Employment \u00a0 Flinders University is proud to be an organisation that is committed to our Reconciliation Action Plan and Indigenous Workforce Strategy. Our vision is to be a preferred employer for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples.\u00a0 We are committed to progressing Indigenous advancement in education, research, employment, and wellbeing, and strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all Flinders vacancies. \u00a0 Please see here for our Reconciliation Action Plan \u00a0 Please see here for our Indigenous Workforce Strategy \u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0 Prescribed Conditions for Employment \u00a0 Appointment to this role is conditional on the completion of required pre-employment checks and declarations, each of which must be satisfactory to the University. These include: \u00a0 Flinders University will require a current completed Nationally Coordinated Criminal History Check and Gender Based Violence Declaration which is satisfactory to the University. The contract of Employment is conditional upon the receipt of these completed compliance checks. A disclosable outcome will not automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration. Each case will be assessed on its individual merits and relevance to the inherent requirements of the role. In addition, it is a requirement of this position that the incumbent maintain a current Working with Children Check which is satisfactory to the University in accordance with the Child Safety (Prohibited Persons) Act 2016 (SA). SA: Staff working in a health care setting are strongly recommended to be fully vaccinated against COVID-19 in line with the SA Health policy.\u00a0 \u00a0 How to Apply and Information You are required to submit a CV, along with a Suitability Statement as a separate document.\u00a0 This should be no more than 3 pages, and address the Key Position Capabilities of the View Position Description \u2013 Lecturer Teaching Specialist (Clinical Practitioner) View Position Description \u2013 Senior Lecturer Teaching Specialist (Clinical Practitioner)\u00a0 Flinders University is committed to providing an environment where staff with disability are valued, supported and encouraged to participate fully and independently in the life of the University.\u00a0If you require any reasonable adjustments to assist you in the selection process, please advise the contact in the Recruitment Team so that we can make appropriate arrangements through recruitment@flinders.edu.au or call 08 8201 2383. For more information regarding this position, please contact Professor Chris Barr Certification Applications to be submitted before 10.00pm: 22 Oct 2026 At Flinders we embrace and celebrate diversity and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people of all ages, ethnicities, abilities, sexual orientations, and gender identities. Flinders. Fearless."}, "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Bedford-Park--Kaurna-Country/Research-Associate-in-Marine-Biology--Biofouling---Molecular-Ecology-_JR0000017701-1": {"title": "Research Associate in Marine Biology (Biofouling & Molecular Ecology)", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-02\nFull time\n\nPosition Details Full-Time | Two-year contract Academic Level A | $90,930 - $110,197 pa Location: Bedford Park / Kaurna Country View Position Description About the Role We are seeking an enthusiastic and highly motivated Research Associate to join the ARC Training Centre for Biofilm Research & Innovation (BRIC) and contribute to an exciting research project investigating biofouling communities in Australian waters. Working under the direction of the Chief Investigator and in collaboration with project and partner investigators, you will play a key role in designing, managing and delivering research activities for the project. In this position, your duties will include, but not be limited to: Leading research investigating the establishment of marine biofouling communities on artificial structures. Apply advanced molecular and bioinformatic techniques to assess the diversity, composition, and temporal dynamics of biofouling communities. Design, conduct and analyse experiments examining biofouling processes on marine infrastructure. Contribute to the development of research methodologies, experimental protocols, and sampling strategies to support project objectives. Work collaboratively with an interdisciplinary team of researchers and project partners, including government agencies and industry stakeholders. Interpret and communicate research findings through technical reports, scientific publications, presentations, and stakeholder engagement activities. Assist with project management activities, including planning, data management, reporting, and achievement of project milestones. This position is open to candidates with Australian working rights. Relocation support may be available for the successful candidate. About You You will be passionate about protecting Australia\u2019s marine environments and advancing the sustainable management of its oceans and waterways. You will be a collaborative, proactive and motivated researcher with a strong interest in marine biofouling, molecular ecology or a related field, committed to delivering high-quality, impactful research. As well as completion (or near-completion) of a PhD in Marine Biology or Marine Genomics or Marine Microbiology or Bioinformatics, you should demonstrate; Research experience in biofouling, marine invasive species, marine microbial ecology, or related fields. Knowledge of marine organism identification and taxonomy, particularly in relation to biofouling communities. A growing research profile in marine microbial ecology, molecular ecology, metagenomics, or a closely related discipline, evidenced by publications and other research outputs. Experience applying molecular and microbiological techniques, including genomic and metagenomic approaches, to address ecological research questions. Expertise in bioinformatic analyses and the interpretation of complex biological and ecological datasets. Demonstrated skills in quantitative data analysis, including proficiency in R, Python, MATLAB, or equivalent software. Strong interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to work effectively both independently and collaboratively within multidisciplinary research teams. \u00a0 About the ARC Training Centre for Biofilm Research and Innovation\u00a0 We are the leading Australian research and training centre tackling biofilm-related challenges. \u00a0 The ARC Training Centre for Biofilm Research and Innovation , led by Flinders University, is a 5 year, $7.8m research and training program, bringing together 5 universities, 10 industry partners and key industry and regulatory bodies to deliver innovative research and biofilm solutions to tackle important issues for the maritime and water industries.\u00a0 Biofilms grow on all surfaces and environments, from catheters to drinking water pipes and ships. They are complex organisations of cells that grow on both living and inert surfaces and are both viscous and elastic in nature. They can be made up of a single species or comprise several species of different types of microorganisms, including those that pose a threat to either human health or our environment. Biofilm attachment and development cannot be prevented completely thus they cost billions each year to those attempting to eradicate them.\u00a0 \u00a0 By working with industries to develop innovative solutions that meet their needs and alleviate their biofilm-related problems, the ARC Training Centre for Biofilm Research and Innovation aims to: transform biofouling management strategies for maritime platforms; train the next generation of interdisciplinary scientists and engineers; and to develop biofilm management strategies across the defence and water industries to address evolving regulatory stringency.\u00a0 Life at Flinders They say know your place.\u00a0 We say you've found it right here. Flinders University was founded on the belief that learning should open minds, celebrate individuality and give people the freedom to pursue their own point of view. That spirit lives on in our community of thinkers, doers and changemakers who challenge convention, and each other, to shape what comes next. Rising to a challenge is nothing new for Flinders. During our first 60 years, we\u2019ve navigated revolutionary changes in social and cultural norms, and have responded to transformative economic, environmental and technological developments. Through it all, we\u2019ve continued to deliver for our students and community, innovating in learning and research to prepare graduates for the changing world they help create. Reaching beyond the limits of buildings, borders, and backgrounds, ours is an inclusive culture that believes absolutely in equality and opportunity for all. We don't just accommodate differences; we embrace and celebrate them. \u00a0 So, \u00a0 why work at Flinders? \u00a0 17% Superannuation + salary packaging options Flexible working arrangements Awarded the AHEIA Higher Education Award for Workplace Culture Excellence due to our commitment to wellbeing through our Thriving@Flinders staff wellbeing program Wide range of professional development activities and services, including exclusive staff study offers\u00a0 We embrace diversity and promote equity and inclusion for all students and staff, as shown through our three SAGE Cygnet Awards. Vibrant campus life and amenities including on campus\u00a0 health care services ,\u00a0 gym \u00a0and\u00a0 childcare centre (Bedford Park, South Australia). \u00a0 Prescribed Conditions for Employment Appointment to this role is conditional on the completion of required pre-employment checks and declarations, each of which must be satisfactory to the University. \u00a0 These include: Flinders University will require a current completed Nationally Coordinated Criminal History Check and Gender Based Violence Declaration which is satisfactory to the University. The contract of Employment is conditional upon the receipt of these completed compliance checks. A disclosable outcome will not automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration. Each case will be assessed on its individual merits and relevance to the inherent requirements of the role. The successful candidate will be required to obtain a baseline Security Clearance. \u00a0 \u00a0 How to Apply and Information You are required to submit a CV, along with a Suitability Statement as a separate document.\u00a0 This should be no more than 3 pages, and address the Key Position Capabilities of the position description . For more information regarding this position, please contact the Recruitment team via email at For more information regarding this position, please contact the Recruitment team via email at For more information regarding this position, please contact the Recruitment team via email at recruitment@flinders.edu.au or phone (08) 8201 2383. \u00a0 Applications to be submitted before 10:00 pm (ACDT) on Sunday, 25 October 2026. Please note, late applications and applications sent via agencies will not be accepted . At Flinders we embrace and celebrate diversity and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people of all ages, ethnicities, abilities, sexual orientations, and gender identities. Certification Applications to be submitted before 10.00pm: 25 Oct 2026 At Flinders we embrace and celebrate diversity and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people of all ages, ethnicities, abilities, sexual orientations, and gender identities. Flinders. Fearless."}, "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Bedford-Park--Kaurna-Country/Social-Media-Officer_JR0000017752": {"title": "Social Media Officer", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nPart time\n\nPart-Time at 0.5 FTE | Fixed term (12 months)\u00a0 Higher Education Officer Level 5 | $84,599 - $93,366\u00a0(pro-rata) Location: Bedford Park / Kaurna Country \u00a0 View Position Description \u00a0 \u00a0 This is a unique opportunity for someone who possess native-level written and spoken communication skills in Mandarin Chinese and advanced English communication skills to work with Flinders Marketing and Student Recruitment Team. \u00a0 About the Role \u00a0 Ready to create content that reaches and inspires future students across one of China's most popular social media platforms? As the Social Media Officer (Chinese Channels), you'll help grow Flinders University's presence in China through engaging content, online community building, and digital campaigns that connect with prospective students. \u00a0 In this role, you will be responsible for: Creating and sharing engaging content across Chinese social media channels, with a strong focus on Xiaohongshu (RED). Building and maintaining active online communities by responding to audiences and encouraging engagement. Tracking social media performance and using insights to improve content and grow audiences. Collaborating with colleagues across the University to showcase student stories and support international student recruitment. \u00a0 For more information on the key position responsibilities, please see the position description \u00a0 This position makes a significant contribution to the University\u2019s strategic plan, \u201cChanging 10 million lives, Every One Matters\u201d by 2035, by building awareness of Flinders University among prospective students in China through engaging social media content. The role supports Flinders\u2019 commitment to being student-centred, fostering a vibrant culture through storytelling, and driving innovation through the effective use of digital and social media platforms. \u00a0 About You \u00a0 You are a creative and motivated social media professional who understands Chinese social media and what audiences enjoy seeing online. You can create great content, build engagement, and use data to improve results. \u00a0 To succeed in this role, you will have: Experience creating high-quality social media content, including videos, photography and written posts. Strong understanding of Chinese social media platforms, particularly Xiaohongshu (RED), trends and audience interests. Native-level written and spoken communication skills in both Mandarin Chinese and English. Ability to review social media results, identifying opportunities for improvement and managing multiple tasks effectively. \u00a0 About the Marketing and Student Recruitment team\u00a0 \u00a0 The Marketing and Student Recruitment team is evolving in 2026 with exciting new opportunities at our vibrant Bedford Park campus and the cutting-edge Flinders City Campus. As we accelerate our growth ambitions, we are looking for skilled and motivated team members to help drive our marketing strategies and initiatives. If you are passionate about shaping impactful marketing campaigns, building the Flinders University brand, and contributing to the recruitment of future students, we want to hear from you. \u00a0 Join us in a team that is focused on innovation, excellence, and delivering results that will position Flinders as a leader in higher education.\u00a0 \u00a0 Life at Flinders \u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0 They say know your place.\u00a0 We say you've found it right here.\u00a0 \u00a0 Flinders University was founded on the belief that learning should open minds, celebrate individuality and give people the freedom to pursue their own point of view. That spirit lives on in our community of thinkers, doers and changemakers who challenge convention, and each other, to shape what comes next.\u00a0 \u00a0 Rising to a challenge is nothing new for Flinders. During our first 60 years, we\u2019ve navigated revolutionary changes in social and cultural norms, and have responded to transformative economic, environmental and technological developments. Through it all, we\u2019ve continued to deliver for our students and community, innovating in learning and research to prepare graduates for the changing world they help create.\u00a0 \u00a0 Reaching beyond the limits of buildings, borders, and backgrounds, ours is an inclusive culture that believes absolutely in equality and opportunity for all. We don't just accommodate differences; we embrace and celebrate them.\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0 So,\u202f why work at Flinders? \u00a0 17% Superannuation + salary packaging options\u00a0\u00a0 Flexible working arrangements\u00a0\u00a0 Awarded the AHEIA Higher Education Award for Workplace Culture Excellence due to our\u00a0commitment to wellbeing through our\u00a0 Thriving@Flinders \u00a0staff wellbeing program\u00a0 Wide range of professional development activities and\u00a0services, including exclusive staff study offers\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 We embrace diversity and promote equity and inclusion for all students and staff, as shown through our three SAGE Cygnet Awards.\u00a0\u00a0 Vibrant campus life and amenities including on campus\u202f health care services ,\u202f gym \u202fand\u202f childcare centre\u00a0 (Bedford Park, South Australia).\u00a0\u00a0 Recognised as a Veteran Employer of Choice\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0 Our Commitment to Reconciliation and Indigenous Employment \u00a0 Flinders University is proud to be an organisation that is committed to our Reconciliation Action Plan and Indigenous Workforce Strategy. Our vision is to be a preferred employer for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples.\u00a0 We are committed to progressing Indigenous advancement in education, research, employment, and wellbeing, and strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all Flinders vacancies.\u00a0\u00a0 Please see here for our\u00a0 Reconciliation Action Plan \u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Please see here for our\u00a0 Indigenous Workforce Strategy \u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Prescribed Conditions for Employment \u00a0 Appointment to this role is conditional on the completion of required pre-employment checks and declarations, each of which must be satisfactory to the University.\u00a0\u00a0This includes: A\u00a0current\u00a0completed\u00a0Nationally Coordinated Criminal History Check\u00a0and Gender Based Violence\u00a0Declaration\u00a0which is satisfactory to the University. The contract of Employment is conditional upon\u00a0the receipt of these\u00a0completed compliance checks.\u00a0A\u00a0disclosable outcome\u00a0will not automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration. Each case will be assessed on its individual merits and relevance to the inherent requirements of the role.\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0 How to Apply and Information \u00a0 You are required to submit a CV, along with a Cover Letter as a separate document, telling us a little about yourself, and why you feel you are suited to this role. Flinders University\u00a0is\u00a0committed\u00a0to providing an environment where staff with disability are valued, supported and encouraged\u00a0to\u00a0participate fully and independently in the life of the University.\u202fIf you require any reasonable adjustments to assist you in the selection process, please advise\u00a0the contact\u00a0in\u00a0the Recruitment Team\u00a0so that we can make appropriate arrangements\u00a0through\u00a0 recruitment@flinders.edu.au \u00a0or call\u00a008 8201 2383.\u00a0 For more information regarding this position, please contact\u00a0 Laura Logan \u00a0 Certification Applications to be submitted before 10.00pm: 25 Oct 2026 At Flinders we embrace and celebrate diversity and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people of all ages, ethnicities, abilities, sexual orientations, and gender identities. Flinders. Fearless."}, "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Bedford-Park--Kaurna-Country/Procurement-Category-Manager_JR0000017110": {"title": "Procurement Category Manager", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nFull time\n\nPosition Details \u00a0 Full-Time\u00a0| Fixed term (15 months) HEO9 - $133,860 + 17% Super Location: Bedford Park / Kaurna Country View Position Description\u00a0 \u00a0 About the Role \u00a0 The Procurement Category Manager at Flinders University is responsible for the procurement and contracting of specified major commodity groups across the University, or for specific high-risk procurement projects.\u00a0 The role involves developing an in-depth understanding of the University stakeholder requirements including extensive consultation with user groups and leading cross functional teams to deliver exceptional procurement outcomes. This may include being responsible for the creation or review of some or all documentation related to the procurement process and ensuring that appropriate changes and updates are made to Flinders University systems as well as procedures and guidelines. Working in this impactful role will involve: Developing procurement strategies to meet the commercial imperative of the University as well as stakeholder requirements, incorporating overall market approach, proposed contract type, scope and length. Undertaking procurement processes to achieve strategic outcomes, including preparing Acquisition Plans, undertaking market approaches, evaluation and recommendations, and all Governance reporting. Establishing and leading cross functional teams of stakeholders and/or functional experts as appropriate to undertake processes, including evaluations.\u00a0 Ensuring stakeholders are appropriately engaged and managed. Ensuring project management protocols are maintained, and that appropriate reporting occurs with regards to progress, risks and issues. Please note, due to the nature of the role, you will be required to work from the Bedford Park campus. About You \u00a0 We are looking for a skilled and personable procurement professional with: Experience in the development of procurement documentation including approvals documentation and market approach documentation. Well developed commercial sense, including negotiation of contracts and the drafting of contracts High level oral, written and interpersonal communication skills including being an effective listener and negotiator, being able to ask clear questions about issues and requirements, and experience in writing quality reports and recommendations for complex and sensitive issues. Proficiency in the identification, development and implementation of procurement strategies for a range of category groups or specific projects Demonstrated experience of managing a complex end to end procurement process from identification of customer needs through to contract execution and contract handover. About Finance and Procurement Services\u00a0 Finance and Procurement Services assist the University to achieve its goals by providing quality leadership, information, and financial services. The Finance and Procurement Services team undertakes monthly financial management reporting and forecasting, annual budgets and monitoring performance against these budgets, all regulatory financial reporting, monthly compliance, procurement contracting and functional areas of paying suppliers, receipting revenue and annual financial statements.\u00a0 While this role is based at Bedford Park, we have team members located across all of Flinders sites. Life at Flinders We're transforming and investing in people and facilities to create contemporary, stimulating, and satisfying learning and work environments that reflect our core values of excellence, innovation, courage, and integrity. Flinders is refocusing its strategic priorities with the aim of elevating its performance to be a top ten Australian university, and amongst the top 1% in the world. Reaching beyond the limits of buildings, borders, and backgrounds, ours is an inclusive culture that believes absolutely in equality and opportunity for all. We don't just accommodate differences; we embrace and celebrate them. So,\u00a0 why work at Flinders? 17% Superannuation + salary packaging options\u00a0\u00a0 Our commitment to wellbeing through our Thriving@Flinders initiative\u00a0 Wide range of professional development activities and services, including exclusive staff study offers\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 We embrace diversity and promote equity and inclusion for all students and staff, as shown through our three SAGE Cygnet Awards.\u00a0\u00a0 Vibrant campus life and amenities including on campus\u202f health care services ,\u202f gym \u202fand\u202f childcare centre (Bedford Park, South Australia).\u00a0\u00a0 Our Commitment to Reconciliation and Indigenous Employment \u00a0 Flinders University is proud to be an organisation that is committed to our Reconciliation Action Plan and Indigenous Workforce Strategy. Our vision is to be a preferred employer for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples.\u00a0 We are committed to progressing Indigenous advancement in education, research, employment, and wellbeing, and strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all Flinders vacancies.\u00a0 Please see here for our Reconciliation Action Plan \u00a0\u00a0 Please see here for our Indigenous Workforce Strategy \u00a0 Prescribed Conditions for Employment A current Nationally Coordinated Criminal History Check which is satisfactory to the University will be required by Flinders University before the successful applicant can commence in this position . A criminal record will not automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration. Each case will be assessed on its individual merits and relevance to the inherent requirements of the role. \u00a0 How to Apply and Information \u00a0 In addition to uploading your CV, please submit a separate Suitability Statement of no more than 3 pages, addressing the key position capabilities of the Position Description. For more information regarding this position, please contact Deborah Ashdown Applications will be considered as they are received. To avoid disappointment, we encourage applicants to submit their application as soon as possible, as we may close the advertisement early should a suitable candidate be identified. If you have previously applied for this position, there is no need to submit another application. Certification Applications to be submitted before 10.00pm: 25 Oct 2026 At Flinders we embrace and celebrate diversity and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people of all ages, ethnicities, abilities, sexual orientations, and gender identities. Flinders. Fearless."}, "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Bedford-Park--Kaurna-Country/Senior-Network-Services-Officer_JR0000017747": {"title": "Senior Network Services Officer", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nFull time\n\nPosition Details Full-Time | Continuing Higher Education Officer Level 6 | $94,456 - $100,710 Location: Bedford Park / Kaurna Country View Position Description \u00a0 About the Role We're looking for someone with a strong foundation in networking who is curious, adaptable, and enjoys being part of a team. \u00a0 While experience is valued, attitude is paramount. We want someone who is keen to learn, willing to get involved across infrastructure and technology domains when needed, and comfortable rolling up their sleeves to solve problems wherever they arise. This role is ideal for someone who sees every challenge as an opportunity to learn, improve, and contribute. \u00a0 The Network Engineer plays a key role in the delivery, support, and continuous improvement of the University's network infrastructure and connectivity services. Working within the Cloud & Infrastructure Services team, you will help maintain reliable, secure, and scalable network services that support teaching, learning, research, and business operations across the University. \u00a0 This is a hands-on technical role that will suit an engineer who enjoys solving problems, working collaboratively, and contributing beyond their core area of expertise when required. \u00a0 As the Senior Network Services Officer, you will be responsible for: Supporting the delivery, management and continuous improvement of the University's network services and infrastructure. Contributing to the implementation of network technology strategies, projects and roadmap initiatives. Partnering with stakeholders to provide technical expertise and enhance customer-focused network services. Identifying and mitigating risks, while monitoring emerging technologies and supporting best-practice network operations. \u00a0 A more comprehensive list of duties is available from the Position Description \u00a0 This position makes a significant contribution to the University\u2019s strategic plan to \u201cChanging 10 million lives, Every One Matters\u201d, by 2035 through the delivery of secure, reliable and future-focused network services that enable teaching, research and operations across the University. The role supports a culture of innovation, continuous improvement and agile ways of working to meet evolving technology and business needs. \u00a0 About You \u00a0 To be successful in this role, you will demonstrate: Relevant qualifications in Information Technology (or a related discipline) and/or equivalent experience in a technical IT environment. Experience in one or more areas including routing protocols, network troubleshooting, switching architectures, network security, firewalls, VPNs or multi-vendor network environments. Strong analytical, planning and problem-solving skills, with the ability to identify and deliver effective technical solutions. Excellent communication and stakeholder engagement skills, coupled with experience working collaboratively in agile or matrix-based environments. \u00a0 Experience within the higher education sector and/or Cisco networking environments, including CCNA certification or equivalent experience, will be highly regarded. \u00a0 What We're Looking For \u00a0 You are a technically capable network professional with strong analytical and problem-solving skills, a customer-focused approach and a genuine desire to continuously develop your expertise. You enjoy working collaboratively, building effective relationships with stakeholders and contributing to the delivery of reliable, high-quality technology services. \u00a0 Why Join the Team? \u00a0 We're building a team of people who are collaborative, adaptable, and willing to help wherever needed. While networking is the primary focus of this role, we are looking for someone who understands that delivering great technology outcomes is a team sport. \u00a0 If you're the type of person who enjoys learning, isn't afraid to step outside your comfort zone, and wants exposure to a broad range of infrastructure technologies, we'd love to hear from you. \u00a0 Technical skills can be learned. Curiosity, initiative, teamwork, and attitude are what make great engineers. Opportunity to work with modern cloud, network, and security technologies \u00a0 What Success Looks Like \u00a0 After 12 months in this role, you will have: Become a trusted member of the Infrastructure Services team. Built a strong understanding of the University's network and technology environment. Contributed to service improvements and infrastructure projects. Developed skills beyond traditional networking into cloud, security, and platform technologies. Established strong working relationships across IDS and the broader University. \u00a0 This is an excellent opportunity for a network engineer who wants more than \"just networking\" and is looking to grow into a well-rounded infrastructure professional \u00a0 Life at Flinders \u00a0 They say know your place.\u00a0\u00a0We say\u00a0you've\u00a0found it right here.\u00a0 Flinders University was founded on the belief that learning should open minds, celebrate\u00a0individuality\u00a0and give people the freedom to pursue their own point of view. That spirit lives on in our community of thinkers, doers and changemakers who challenge convention, and each other, to shape what comes next.\u00a0 Rising to a challenge is nothing new for Flinders. During our first 60 years,\u00a0we\u2019ve\u00a0navigated revolutionary changes in social and cultural norms, and have responded to transformative economic,\u00a0environmental\u00a0and technological developments. Through it all,\u00a0we\u2019ve\u00a0continued to deliver for our students and community, innovating in learning and research to prepare graduates for the changing world they help create.\u00a0 Reaching beyond the limits of buildings, borders, and backgrounds, ours is an inclusive culture that believes absolutely in equality and opportunity for all. We\u00a0don't\u00a0just accommodate differences; we embrace and celebrate them.\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0 Our Commitment to Reconciliation and Indigenous Employment \u00a0 Flinders University is proud to be an organisation that is committed to our Reconciliation Action Plan and Indigenous Workforce Strategy. Our vision is to be a preferred employer for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples.\u00a0\u00a0We are committed to progressing Indigenous advancement in education, research, employment, and wellbeing, and strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all Flinders vacancies.\u00a0\u00a0 Please see here for\u00a0our\u00a0 Reconciliation Action Plan \u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Please see here for\u00a0our\u00a0 Indigenous Workforce Strategy \u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0 Prescribed Conditions for Employment \u00a0 Appointment to this role is conditional on the completion of required pre-employment checks and declarations, each of which must be satisfactory to the University. This includes: A current completed Nationally Coordinated Criminal History Check and Gender Based Violence Declaration which is satisfactory to the University. The contract of Employment is conditional upon the receipt of these completed compliance checks. A disclosable outcome will not automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration. Each case will be assessed on its individual merits and relevance to the inherent requirements of the role. \u00a0 How to Apply and Information You are required to submit a CV, along with a Suitability Statement of no more than 3 pages, addressing the below Key Position Capabilities of the Position Description : Well-developed thinking, planning and analytical skills. Well-developed self-improvement and growth mindset/approach to the role and as part of a wider team. Well-developed interpersonal influence and demonstrated ability to negotiate and communicate effectively with staff and customers across a diverse organisation particularly during the design, management and implementation of customer solutions. Cisco Certified Network Associate (CCNA) certification or demonstrated experience in configuring or managing a CISCO Environment. Well-developed experience in at least one of current routing protocols, network troubleshooting techniques, a multi-vendor/multi-protocol environment, modern switching architectures, structured cabling standards and network security environments, including but not limited to firewalls and VPNs. Flinders University is committed to providing an environment where staff with disability are valued, supported and encouraged to participate fully and independently in the life of the University.\u202fIf you require any reasonable adjustments to assist you in the selection process, please advise the contact in the Recruitment Team so that we can make appropriate arrangements through recruitment@flinders.edu.au or call 08 8201 2383. For more information regarding this position, please contact Warren Pearse Certification National Police Certificate - Australian Federal Police Applications to be submitted before 10.00pm: 25 Oct 2026 At Flinders we embrace and celebrate diversity and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people of all ages, ethnicities, abilities, sexual orientations, and gender identities. Flinders. Fearless."}, "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Bedford-Park--Kaurna-Country/HDR-Engagement-Senior-Support-Officer_JR0000017724": {"title": "HDR Engagement Senior Support Officer", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-07\nFull time\n\nPosition Details 5-Years Fixed Term I Full Time Higher Education Officer Level 6 I $94,456\u00a0-\u00a0$100,710 + 17% Super Location: Bedford Park / Kaurna Country View Position Description A Role with Impact: The HDR Engagement Senior Support Officer is a key role within the Office of Graduate Research (OGR), providing high-level administrative, project and stakeholder support for national and international Higher Degree by Research (HDR) engagement and partnership activities. \u00a0 Working closely with the Dean of Graduate Research, HDR Strategic Operations and Quality Assurance Partner, College HDR Coordinators and the HDR Engagement and Partnerships Manager, you will support initiatives including cotutelle arrangements, industry internships, scholarships and the National Industry PhD Program. You will coordinate projects, reporting, committees and events while providing advice and support to HDR students, supervisors and internal and external stakeholders. \u00a0 The HDR Engagement Senior Support Officer will: Support HDR engagement and partnership initiatives, including cotutelles, internships, industry scholarships and the National Industry PhD Program. Coordinate projects, reporting, committees and events that support national and international HDR engagement and partnership activities. Provide advice and high-quality support to HDR students, supervisors and stakeholders on relevant policies, procedures and engagement opportunities. Build strong relationships and contribute to continuous improvement, working across Colleges, professional services and external industry partners to enhance HDR engagement and services \u00a0 About You You are an organised, collaborative and highly capable professional with experience providing administrative, project or coordination support, ideally within the higher education sector. \u00a0 You bring strong attention to detail, excellent communication skills and the ability to manage multiple priorities while delivering high-quality outcomes. You are confident interpreting policies and procedures, working with a diverse range of stakeholders and providing professional advice and support in a complex environment. \u00a0 You demonstrate: Experience providing high-level administrative, project or coordination support, preferably within higher education, research partnerships or industry engagement. The ability to interpret, apply and provide advice on complex policies, procedures and guidelines, with strong attention to detail and accuracy. Experience working with databases and complex information systems, together with strong Microsoft Office skills. An understanding of current issues affecting the higher education sector, particularly HDR engagement, research partnerships and industry collaboration. \u00a0 About the Office of Graduate Research: The Office of Graduate Research (OGR) supports the success, development and impact of Flinders University\u2019s Higher Degree by Research (HDR) community. Our experienced team provides expert support across the HDR lifecycle, from admissions, progression and examination through to research training, employability, industry engagement, international opportunities and supervisor development. We are committed to creating an exceptional HDR experience, fostering research excellence and connecting our researchers with opportunities to make a meaningful impact. \u00a0 Life at Flinders They say know your place.\u00a0 We say you've found it right here. Flinders University was founded on the belief that learning should open minds, celebrate individuality and give people the freedom to pursue their own point of view. That spirit lives on in our community of thinkers, doers and changemakers who challenge convention, and each other, to shape what comes next. Reaching beyond the limits of buildings, borders, and backgrounds, ours is an inclusive culture that believes absolutely in equality and opportunity for all. We don't just accommodate differences; we embrace and celebrate them. So,\u00a0 why work at Flinders? 17% Superannuation + salary packaging options Flexible working arrangements Awarded the AHEIA Higher Education Award for Workplace Culture Excellence due to our commitment to wellbeing through our\u00a0 Thriving@Flinders \u00a0staff wellbeing program Wide range of professional development activities and services, including exclusive staff study offers\u00a0 We embrace diversity and promote equity and inclusion for all students and staff, as shown through our three SAGE Cygnet Awards. Vibrant campus life and amenities including on campus\u00a0 health care services ,\u00a0 gym \u00a0and\u00a0 childcare centre (Bedford Park, South Australia). Recognised as a Veteran Employer of Choice\u00a0 Our Commitment to Reconciliation and Indigenous Employment Flinders University is proud to be an organisation that is committed to our Reconciliation Action Plan and Indigenous Workforce Strategy. Our vision is to be a preferred employer for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples.\u00a0 We are committed to progressing Indigenous advancement in education, research, employment, and wellbeing, and strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all Flinders vacancies. Please see here for our Reconciliation Action Plan Please see here for our Indigenous Workforce Strategy Prescribed Conditions for Employment A current Nationally Coordinated Criminal History Check which is satisfactory to the University will be required by Flinders University before the successful applicant can commence in this position. A criminal record will not automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration. Each case will be assessed on its individual merits and relevance to the inherent requirements of the role. \u00a0 How to Apply and Information As well as a CV, you are required to submit a Suitability Statement of no more than 3 pages, addressing the below four Key Position Capabilities of the position description : Demonstrated ability to interpret, apply and provide advice on complex policies, procedures and guidelines. Strong attention to detail, accuracy, and demonstrated ability to deliver very high standards of work relating to research partnerships and/or industry engagement. Proficiency in working with a complex database such as a student management information system. Experience and/or a demonstrated understanding of the current issues impacting on the higher education sector, particularly as pertains to HDR engagement and partnership activities. For more information regarding this position, please contact Professor Lucy Lewis . Applications to be submitted before 10:00 pm (ACDT) on Sunday, 25 October 2026. Please note, late applications and applications sent via agencies will not be accepted . At Flinders we embrace and celebrate diversity and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people of all ages, ethnicities, abilities, sexual orientations, and gender identities. Certification Applications to be submitted before 10.00pm: 25 Oct 2026 At Flinders we embrace and celebrate diversity and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people of all ages, ethnicities, abilities, sexual orientations, and gender identities. Flinders. Fearless."}, "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Bedford-Park--Kaurna-Country/Senior-Risk-Audit-Specialist_JR0000017714": {"title": "Senior Risk and Audit Specialist", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-06\nFull time\n\nPosition Details \u00a0 Full-Time\u00a0| Continuing Higher Education Officer Level 8\u00a0|\u00a0$116,349 - $128,806 Location:\u00a0 Bedford Park / Kaurna Country \u00a0 View Position Description \u00a0 About the Role \u00a0 We are seeking a highly capable Senior Risk and Audit Specialist to join Information and Digital Services (IDS) at Flinders University. Reporting to the Senior Information Security Audit & Risk Lead, you will play a key role in strengthening governance, risk and compliance practices across a complex and evolving digital environment. \u00a0 Working closely with IDS leaders and stakeholders across the University, you will support the ongoing development and continuous improvement of risk and governance frameworks, policies and processes. You will provide expert guidance on risk, audit and compliance activities, contribute to governance reporting, and help ensure strategic and operational initiatives align with best practice governance standards. This is an excellent opportunity for a governance and risk professional who enjoys influencing outcomes, building strong relationships and driving continuous improvement within a collaborative and forward-thinking team. \u00a0 Key responsibilities include: Supporting the development and continuous improvement of IDS governance and risk frameworks, policies, processes and standards. Providing advice, reporting and support to governance forums, leadership teams and stakeholders to strengthen risk, audit and compliance outcomes. Collaborating with IDS teams to ensure audit, risk and compliance activities align with operational priorities and strategic objectives. Contributing to the development and management of governance, risk, audit and compliance models that support informed decision-making and prioritisation. Undertaking secretariat responsibilities for key IDS governance committees and coordinating associated actions, communications and initiatives. \u00a0 For a more comprehensive list of duties, please see the Position Description. \u00a0 About You \u00a0 You are an experienced governance, risk or audit professional who enjoys bringing structure, insight and continuous improvement to complex environments. You have a collaborative approach, strong stakeholder engagement skills and the ability to balance strategic thinking with operational delivery. You are motivated by the opportunity to influence positive outcomes and help strengthen governance and risk practices across a large and complex organisation. \u00a0 To be successful in this role, you will demonstrate: Significant experience in governance, risk, audit or compliance roles within a complex environment. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to identify risks and deliver practical recommendations. Excellent communication and stakeholder management skills, with the ability to influence and build effective working relationships. Experience developing, implementing or supporting governance frameworks, risk management processes and reporting activities. Relevant postgraduate qualifications and/or an equivalent combination of education, training and professional experience. \u00a0 About\u00a0Information and Digital Services \u00a0 Information and Digital Services (IDS) are a pivotal resource of the University, providing information and digital technology services and support to the Flinders University staff and student community. The IDS team apply technical expertise to support university projects and provide core services such as the IDS Service Desk, Audio visual, simulation and event services, Information security and identity access management services and more. \u00a0 Life at Flinders \u00a0 They say know your place.\u00a0 We say you've found it right here. \u00a0 Flinders University was founded on the belief that learning should open minds, celebrate individuality and give people the freedom to pursue their own point of view. That spirit lives on in our community of thinkers, doers and changemakers who challenge convention, and each other, to shape what comes next.\u00a0 \u00a0 Rising to a challenge is nothing new for Flinders. During our first 60 years, we\u2019ve navigated revolutionary changes in social and cultural norms, and have responded to transformative economic, environmental and technological developments. Through it all, we\u2019ve continued to deliver for our students and community, innovating in learning and research to prepare graduates for the changing world they help create.\u00a0 \u00a0 Reaching beyond the limits of buildings, borders, and backgrounds, ours is an inclusive culture that believes absolutely in equality and opportunity for all. We don't just accommodate differences; we embrace and celebrate them.\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0 So,\u202f why work at Flinders? \u00a0 17% Superannuation + salary packaging options\u00a0\u00a0 Flexible working arrangements\u00a0\u00a0 Awarded the AHEIA Higher Education Award for Workplace Culture Excellence due to our\u00a0commitment to wellbeing through our\u00a0 Thriving@Flinders \u00a0staff wellbeing program\u00a0 Wide range of professional development activities and\u00a0services, including exclusive staff study offers\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 We embrace diversity and promote equity and inclusion for all students and staff, as shown through our three SAGE Cygnet Awards.\u00a0\u00a0 Vibrant campus life and amenities including on campus\u202f health care services ,\u202f gym \u202fand\u202f childcare centre\u00a0 (Bedford Park, South Australia).\u00a0\u00a0 Recognised as a Veteran Employer of Choice \u00a0 Our Commitment to Reconciliation and Indigenous Employment \u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0 Flinders University is proud to be an organisation that is committed to our Reconciliation Action Plan and Indigenous Workforce Strategy. Our vision is to be a preferred employer for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples.\u00a0 We are committed to progressing Indigenous advancement in education, research, employment, and wellbeing, and strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all Flinders vacancies.\u00a0\u00a0 Please see here for our\u00a0 Reconciliation Action Plan \u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Please see here for our\u00a0 Indigenous Workforce Strategy \u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Prescribed Conditions for Employment \u00a0 Appointment to this role is conditional on the completion of required pre-employment checks and declarations, each of which must be satisfactory to the University. This includes: A\u00a0current\u00a0completed\u00a0Nationally Coordinated Criminal History Check\u00a0and Gender Based Violence\u00a0Declaration\u00a0which is satisfactory to the University. The contract of Employment is conditional upon\u00a0the receipt of these\u00a0completed compliance checks.\u00a0A\u00a0disclosable outcome\u00a0will not automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration. Each case will be assessed on its individual merits and relevance to the inherent requirements of the role.\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0 How to Apply and Information \u00a0 You are required to submit a CV, along with a Suitability Statement\u00a0as a separate document.\u00a0 This should be no more than 3 pages,\u00a0and\u00a0address\u00a0the\u00a0Key Position Capabilities of the\u00a0 position description Flinders University\u00a0is\u00a0committed\u00a0to providing an environment where staff with disability are valued, supported and encouraged\u00a0to\u00a0participate fully and independently in the life of the University.\u202fIf you require any reasonable adjustments to assist you in the selection process, please advise\u00a0the contact\u00a0in\u00a0the Recruitment Team\u00a0so that we can make appropriate arrangements\u00a0through\u00a0 recruitment@flinders.edu.au \u00a0or call\u00a008 8201 2383.\u00a0 For more information regarding this position, please contact\u00a0 Tristan Bibbo Certification Applications to be submitted before 10.00pm: 20 Oct 2026 At Flinders we embrace and celebrate diversity and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people of all ages, ethnicities, abilities, sexual orientations, and gender identities. Flinders. Fearless."}, "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Bedford-Park--Kaurna-Country/Senior-Lecturer-Lecturer-in-Palliative---End-of-Life-Care_JR0000017710": {"title": "Senior Lecturer/Lecturer in Palliative & End of Life Care", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-06\nFull time\n\nPosition Details Continuing| Full-Time Academic Level B or C | $115,871 - $162,619 p.a. Location: Bedford Park / Kaurna Country View Position Description \u2013 Lecturer Teaching Specialist (Clinical Practitioner) View Position Description \u2013 Senior Lecturer Teaching Specialist (Clinical Practitioner) \u00a0 About the Role/s The Lecturer Teaching Specialist (Clinical Practitioner) will contribute to excellence in teaching and learning across the suite of Palliative & End of Life Care topics in the College of Health and Enablement. The incumbent will be responsible for making an independent contribution to teaching and the scholarship of teaching using innovations in teaching practices and technologies to deliver excellence in teaching. You will have the opportunity to develop teaching materials, deliver lectures/tutorials or other innovative teaching and learning strategies, coordinate topics and support assessment work. Another exciting aspect of this role is the opportunity to concurrently engage in practice in a clinical or community setting to support maintenance of contemporary practice, knowledge and skills. The Senior Lecturer Teaching Specialist (Clinical Practitioner) will provide leadership in delivering excellence in teaching and learning across the suite of Palliative and End-of-life Care topics and courses in the College of Healthcare and Enablement, that enhance the student experience. The role will provide educational leadership; curriculum design and review; delivery innovation; advancements in education technologies; and leadership in ensuring internal and external compliance and accreditation of courses and continuous quality improvement of university-level education. The Senior Lecturer will also be expected to concurrently engage in practice in a clinical or community setting to support maintenance of contemporary practice, knowledge and skills. Please refer to the attached position descriptions for a comprehensive list of roles and responsibilities. This position makes a significant contribution to the University\u2019s strategic plan to changing 10 million lives, Every One Matters, by 2035 through a commitment to a student-centred ethos and to developing creative, enterprising, career-ready graduates prepared to become lifelong contributors to society. \u00a0 About You Lecturer You are passionate about educating the next generation of palliative & end of life care professionals, evident through your track record of clinical leadership, excellence in teaching at a tertiary level, coupled with your contribution to the development, delivery and evaluation of innovative teaching and learning strategies. You also have a good understanding of the nexus between teaching and learning, research, scholarship and practice. \u00a0 Senior Lecturer You have significant and sustained evidence of excellence in teaching performance at a tertiary level, inclusive of simulation and/or clinical setting, as well as student placement and have experience in coordinating and leading the teaching activities of other staff. You bring a strong understanding of the connection between teaching and learning, research, scholarship and professional practice. You are also able to demonstrate a commitment to enhancing teaching excellence through engagement in teaching and learning strategies, scholarly activities, and ongoing professional development in a higher education teaching. \u00a0 In this role/s you will also demonstrate: \u00a0 Completion of a PhD, or other relevant and equivalent qualification and/or experience. Hold and\u00a0maintain\u00a0a current membership with a relevant professional association. An understanding of pedagogical theory and contemporary educational practice relevant to Palliative and End of Life Care. Excellent oral and written communication skills and interpersonal skills, including the demonstrated ability to establish effective relationships with staff, students and industry nationally and/or internationally. \u00a0 \u00a0 College of Health and Enablement\u00a0 \u00a0 At the College of Health and Enablement, we aim to be an innovator in contemporary education producing a safer and more resilient health and social care workforce. Our mission is to improve lives and empower communities, enabling better health and caring in the world through an exceptional student learning experience. At the College, our research mission is about co-creating new knowledge which promotes wellbeing, and better care and support, to individuals and communities across the lifespan. We work proactively with industry partners and professional bodies leading to more employable and innovative graduates. \u00a0 \u00a0 Life at Flinders \u00a0 They say know your place.\u00a0 We say you've found it right here. Flinders University was founded on the belief that learning should open minds, celebrate individuality and give people the freedom to pursue their own point of view. That spirit lives on in our community of thinkers, doers and changemakers who challenge convention, and each other, to shape what comes next. Rising to a challenge is nothing new for Flinders. During our first 60 years, we\u2019ve navigated revolutionary changes in social and cultural norms, and have responded to transformative economic, environmental and technological developments. Through it all, we\u2019ve continued to deliver for our students and community, innovating in learning and research to prepare graduates for the changing world they help create. Reaching beyond the limits of buildings, borders, and backgrounds, ours is an inclusive culture that believes absolutely in equality and opportunity for all. We don't just accommodate differences; we embrace and celebrate them. So, \u00a0 why work at Flinders? \u00a0 17% Superannuation + salary packaging options Flexible working arrangements Awarded the AHEIA Higher Education Award for Workplace Culture Excellence due to our commitment to wellbeing through our Thriving@Flinders staff wellbeing program Wide range of professional development activities and services, including exclusive staff study offers\u00a0 We embrace diversity and promote equity and inclusion for all students and staff, as shown through our three SAGE Cygnet Awards. Vibrant campus life and amenities including on campus \u00a0 health care services ,\u00a0 gym \u00a0 and \u00a0 childcare centre (Bedford Park, South Australia). Recognised as a Veteran Employer of Choice\u00a0 \u00a0 Our Commitment to Reconciliation and Indigenous Employment \u00a0 Flinders University is proud to be an organisation that is committed to our Reconciliation Action Plan and Indigenous Workforce Strategy. Our vision is to be a preferred employer for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples.\u00a0 We are committed to progressing Indigenous advancement in education, research, employment, and wellbeing, and strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all Flinders vacancies. \u00a0 Please see here for our Reconciliation Action Plan \u00a0 Please see here for our Indigenous Workforce Strategy \u00a0 \u00a0 Prescribed Conditions for Employment \u00a0 Appointment to this role is conditional on the completion of required pre-employment checks and declarations, each of which must be satisfactory to the University. These include: \u00a0 Flinders University will require a current completed Nationally Coordinated Criminal History Check and Gender Based Violence Declaration which is satisfactory to the University. The contract of Employment is conditional upon the receipt of these completed compliance checks. A disclosable outcome will not automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration. Each case will be assessed on its individual merits and relevance to the inherent requirements of the role. In addition, it is a requirement of this position that the incumbent maintain a current Working with Children Check which is satisfactory to the University in accordance with the Child Safety (Prohibited Persons) Act 2016 (SA). SA: Staff working in a health care setting are strongly recommended to be fully vaccinated against COVID-19 in line with the SA Health policy. \u00a0 How to Apply and Information You are required to submit a CV, along with a Suitability Statement as a separate document.\u00a0 This should be no more than 3 pages, and address the Key Position Capabilities of the View Position Description \u2013 Lecturer Teaching Specialist (Clinical Practitioner) View Position Description \u2013 Senior Lecturer Teaching Specialist (Clinical Practitioner) Flinders University is committed to providing an environment where staff with disability are valued, supported and encouraged to participate fully and independently in the life of the University.\u00a0If you require any reasonable adjustments to assist you in the selection process, please advise the contact in the Recruitment Team so that we can make appropriate arrangements through recruitment@flinders.edu.au or call 08 8201 2383. For more information regarding this position, please contact Professor Chris Barr Certification Applications to be submitted before 10.00pm: 27 Oct 2026 At Flinders we embrace and celebrate diversity and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people of all ages, ethnicities, abilities, sexual orientations, and gender identities. Flinders. Fearless."}, "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Bedford-Park--Kaurna-Country/Associate-Lecturer---Associate-Professor-in-Nursing_JR0000017812": {"title": "Associate Lecturer - Associate Professor in Nursing", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-16\nFull time\n\nPosition Details Full-Time | Continuing - Multiple Positions Available Academic Level A to Level D | $90,930 - $186,706 p.a. Location: Bedford Park / Kaurna Country View Candidate Brochure About the Roles: Flinders University\u2019s College of Health and Enablement is seeking academics in Nursing , with a varying range of teaching and research experience to add to our diverse teaching cohort and guide us through the next phase of tremendous student growth, from Associate Lecturers through to Associate Professors. These positions will be filled by people with proven educational and research leadership capabilities and expertise (appropriate for the level). In particular, the positions are intended to amplify education, research and practice in Nursing. Within the multiple roles we have available, you will have the opportunity to: Work in the Nursing Simulation Facilities located in the leafy surrounds of Bedford Park and convenient state-of-the-art Adelaide CBD Support Flinders Nursing students Australia-wide and online, expanding your impact further Teach across various contexts: undergraduate & postgraduate courses; online & face-to-face learning embedded with our industry partners Work flexibility across Australia to contribute to our dynamic online teaching programs in Nursing supporting students nationwide. Improve lives, strengthen communities and shape the future of care. The appointments include Teaching Specialist (Academic), (Clinical Practitioner), and (Teaching and Research) roles. These appointments will provide leadership across education, enhancing the student experience, strengthening our reputation, and supporting sustainable student growth. They will also contribute to research and practice, driving growth in research income, capability, and impact. These positions make a significant contribution to the University\u2019s strategic plan to changing 10 million lives, Every One Matters, by 2035 through an ongoing contribution to improved teaching, learning & research outcomes for the university \u00a0 College of Health and Enablement\u00a0 \u00a0 At the College of Health and Enablement, we aim to be an innovator in contemporary education producing a safer and more resilient health and social care workforce. Our mission is to improve lives and empower communities, enabling better health and caring in the world through an exceptional student learning experience. At the College, our research mission is about co-creating new knowledge which promotes wellbeing, and better care and support, to individuals and communities across the lifespan. We work proactively with industry partners and professional bodies leading to more employable and innovative graduates. \u00a0 \u00a0 Life at Flinders \u00a0 They say know your place.\u00a0 We say you've found it right here. Flinders University was founded on the belief that learning should open minds, celebrate individuality and give people the freedom to pursue their own point of view. That spirit lives on in our community of thinkers, doers and changemakers who challenge convention, and each other, to shape what comes next. Rising to a challenge is nothing new for Flinders. During our first 60 years, we\u2019ve navigated revolutionary changes in social and cultural norms, and have responded to transformative economic, environmental and technological developments. Through it all, we\u2019ve continued to deliver for our students and community, innovating in learning and research to prepare graduates for the changing world they help create. Reaching beyond the limits of buildings, borders, and backgrounds, ours is an inclusive culture that believes absolutely in equality and opportunity for all. We don't just accommodate differences; we embrace and celebrate them. So, \u00a0 why work at Flinders? \u00a0 Ranked in the top 2% of universities worldwide 17% Superannuation + salary packaging options Flexible working arrangements Awarded the AHEIA Higher Education Award for Workplace Culture Excellence due to our commitment to wellbeing through our Thriving@Flinders staff wellbeing program Ninety per cent of Flinders research has been ranked at \u2018world standard or above\u2019 by Excellence in Research for Australia (ERA). Wide range of professional development activities, funds and services, such as Flinders University\u2019s Researcher Development and Leadership Programs. Wide range of professional development activities and services, including exclusive staff study offers\u00a0 We embrace diversity and promote equity and inclusion for all students and staff, as shown through our three SAGE Cygnet Awards. Vibrant campus life and amenities including on campus\u00a0 health care services ,\u00a0 gym \u00a0and\u00a0 childcare centre (Bedford Park, South Australia). Recognised as a Veteran Employer of Choice\u00a0 \u00a0 Our Commitment to Reconciliation and Indigenous Employment \u00a0 Flinders University is proud to be an organisation that is committed to our Reconciliation Action Plan and Indigenous Workforce Strategy. Our vision is to be a preferred employer for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples.\u00a0 We are committed to progressing Indigenous advancement in education, research, employment, and wellbeing, and strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all Flinders vacancies. \u00a0 Please see here for our Reconciliation Action Plan \u00a0 Please see here for our Indigenous Workforce Strategy \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 Prescribed Conditions for Employment \u00a0 Appointment to this role is conditional on the completion of required pre-employment checks and declarations, each of which must be satisfactory to the University. \u00a0 These include: \u00a0 Flinders University will require a current completed Nationally Coordinated Criminal History Check and Gender Based Violence Declaration which is satisfactory to the University. The contract of Employment is conditional upon the receipt of these completed compliance checks. A disclosable outcome will not automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration. Each case will be assessed on its individual merits and relevance to the inherent requirements of the role. In addition, it is a requirement of this position that the incumbent maintain a current Working with Children Check which is satisfactory to the University in accordance with the Child Safety (Prohibited Persons) Act 2016 (SA). SA: Staff working in a health care setting are strongly recommended to be fully vaccinated against COVID-19 in line with the SA Health policy. \u00a0 How to Apply and Information You are required to submit a CV, along with a Suitability Statement as a separate document, detailing the position you are applying for.\u00a0 This should be no more than 3 pages, and address the Key Position Capabilities of the View Position Description - Associate Lecturer Teaching Specialist (Clinical Practitioner) View Position Description - Lecturer Teaching Specialist (Clinical Practitioner) View Position Description - Lecturer Teaching & Research (Balanced) View Position Description - Senior Lecturer Teaching Specialist (Academic) View Position Description - Senior Lecturer \u2013 Teaching Specialist Clinical Practitioner View Position Description - Senior Lecturer \u2013 Teaching & Research (Balanced) View Position Description - Associate Professor Teaching Specialist (Academic) View Position Description - Associate Professor Teaching &Research (Balanced) Flinders University is committed to providing an environment where staff with disability are valued, supported and encouraged to participate fully and independently in the life of the University.\u00a0If you require any reasonable adjustments to assist you in the selection process, please advise the contact in the Recruitment Team so that we can make appropriate arrangements through recruitment@flinders.edu.au or call 08 8201 2383. For more information regarding this position, please contact Professor Chris Barr Certification Applications to be submitted before 10.00pm: 08 Nov 2026 At Flinders we embrace and celebrate diversity and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people of all ages, ethnicities, abilities, sexual orientations, and gender identities. Flinders. Fearless."}, "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Bedford-Park--Kaurna-Country/Senior-Research-Contracts-Officer_JR0000017800": {"title": "Senior Research Contracts Officer", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nFull time\n\nPosition Details Continuing I Full Time\u00a0 Higher Education Officer Level 6 | $94,456 - $100,710 pa | 17% Super Higher Education Officer Level 7 | $102,589 - $113,561 pa | 17% Super HEO6 Position Description | HEO7 Position Description Location: Bedford Park / Kaurna Country About the Role: We are seeking a motivated and skilled professional to join our Research Development and Support team. This unique opportunity is being offered at either the HEO6 (Research Contracts Officer) or HEO7 (Senior Research Contracts Officer) level , depending on the successful candidate's experience and qualifications. In the Research Contracts Officer position, your duties will include (but are not limited to): Providing valued support to the Flinders research community in the administration and processing of contracts and agreements for externally sponsored projects, and providing expertise, customer service and timely advice. Reviewing and negotiating the terms and conditions of research related agreements with industry, government, and other research institutions. Working with the other members of the Research Development and Support team to identify, define and resolve issues related to sponsored project contracting activities. Reviewing and providing advice to researchers on contractual obligations, special conditions or restrictions, or programmatic and other deliverables required by specific funding schemes. In addition to the above, in the Senior Research Contracts Officer position, your duties will include (but are not limited to): The administration and processing of strategic, complex and escalated research contracts and agreements. Assisting with supervisory responsibilities, including developing and mentoring members of the Research Contracts team, and providing backfill for management where required. Identifying and implementing innovative process improvements in contract administration and management. \u00a0 About You To be successful in this role, you will have a strong background in contract administration, drafting, or legal review, preferably within a higher education, government, or research-intensive environment. You possess exceptional communication and negotiation skills, with a proven ability to solve complex problems and balance legal risk against strategic institutional goals. To be successful, you will also require: Excellent time management skills and demonstrated ability to prioritise tasks to meet tight deadlines. Contemporary knowledge of compliance requirements for major grant funding schemes including ARC and NHMRC. Ability to work independently and as part of a team, exercise initiative and judgment in interpreting and applying a range of policies and procedures and work with a broad range of stakeholders, such as academic and professional staff. \u00a0 Life at Flinders Flinders University is driven by a bold purpose: to change lives and change the world. Through Agenda 2035 \u2013 Impact. With Purpose. , we are expanding the scale, reach, and ambition of our research to deliver meaningful outcomes for communities, industry, and global health systems. Reaching beyond the limits of buildings, borders, and backgrounds, ours is an inclusive culture that believes absolutely in equality and opportunity for all. We don't just accommodate differences; we embrace and celebrate them. So,\u00a0 why work at Flinders? 17% Superannuation + salary packaging options Flexible working arrangements Wide range of professional development activities and services We embrace diversity and promote equity and inclusion for all students and staff Vibrant campus life and amenities including on campus\u00a0 health care services ,\u00a0 gym and\u00a0 childcare centre\u00a0 (Bedford Park, South Australia). Support future initiatives like the Flinders HealthCARE Centre Our Commitment to Reconciliation and Indigenous Employment Flinders University is proud to be an organisation that is committed to our Reconciliation Action Plan and Indigenous Workforce Strategy. Our vision is to be a preferred employer for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples.\u00a0 We are committed to progressing Indigenous advancement in education, research, employment, and wellbeing, and strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all Flinders vacancies. Please see here for our Reconciliation Action Plan Please see here for our Indigenous Workforce Strategy Prescribed Conditions for Employment Flinders University will require a current completed Nationally Coordinated Criminal History Check and Gender Based Violence Declaration which is satisfactory to the University. The contract of Employment is conditional upon the receipt of these completed compliance checks. A disclosable outcome will not automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration. Each case will be assessed on its individual merits and relevance to the inherent requirements of the role.\u00a0 \u00a0 How to Apply and Information As well as a CV, you are required to submit a Suitability Statement of no more than 3 pages, addressing the following Key Position Capabilities of the position description: Research Contracts Officer : Demonstrated expertise in research contract management and administration, including drafting, negotiating, reviewing and administration of research contracts and other related documents in a complex environment. Well-developed to high level of attention to detail. Ability to work independently and as part of a team, exercise initiative and judgment in interpreting and applying a range of policies and procedures and work with a broad range of stakeholders, such as academic and professional staff. High level verbal and written communication skills. Senior Research Contracts Officer : Demonstrated experience in the management and administration of complex and strategic research contracts, including drafting, negotiating, reviewing, relationship management, and administration of research contracts and other related documents in a complex environment. Demonstrated well developed to high level verbal and written communication skills including high level attention to detail. Demonstrated ability to identify and implement innovative process improvements in contract administration and management. Ability to mentor, coach and develop professional staff. Demonstrated ability to work independently and as part of a team, exercise initiative and judgment in interpreting and applying a range of policies and procedures and working with a broad range of stakeholders, such as academic and professional staff. For more information regarding this position, please contact Sophie Trabilsie . Certification National Police Check - Australian Federal Police, Working With Children Check - Government of South Australia Applications to be submitted before 10.00pm: 01 Nov 2026 At Flinders we embrace and celebrate diversity and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people of all ages, ethnicities, abilities, sexual orientations, and gender identities. Flinders. Fearless."}, "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Bedford-Park--Kaurna-Country/Senior-Lecturer-Medical-Education--Clinical-Practice-and-Simulation-Lead-_JR0000017794": {"title": "Senior Lecturer Medical Education (Clinical Practice and Simulation Lead)", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nFull time\n\nPosition Details Exclusive Continuing | Full-time Position (36.75 hours per week) Academic Level C | $141,370 - $162,619 p.a. Location: Bedford Park / Kaurna Country View Position Description \u00a0 About the Role \u00a0 We are seeking a Senior Lecturer, Medical Education (Clinical Practice and Simulation Lead) provide leadership in delivering excellence in teaching and learning across the suite of medical education topics and courses prominently in the Doctor of Medicine but inclusive of other college courses with a clinical component. This new, continuing position is well suited to a distinguished practitioner who has perfected the translation of clinical knowledge into practice, and is passionate about nurturing the next generation of Medicine students in a hand- on, simulation environment. The successful candidate will primary be responsible for making a significant and wide-ranging contribution to leadership in teaching, curriculum development and scholarship of teaching using innovations in teaching practices and technologies to deliver excellence in teaching. You will also have the opportunity to: Lead the planning, scheduling and evaluation of Clinical skills practice and simulated learning teaching. Play a lead role in the review, renewal, development and design of curricula and courses that are attractive to existing and new cohorts of students and that nurture creativity and critical-thinking skills. Provide support, academic counselling and professional advice to students to support their studies, professional development and career progression. Provide educational leadership and dissemination of best practice, ensuring awareness and utilisation of contemporary education principles. This position makes a significant contribution to the University's strategic plan to change 10 million lives, Every One Matters , by 2035 through the Strategic Driver of Students First. The primary focus of this role is to design and integrate clinical skills, clinical reasoning and patient assessment activities across curriculum to in turn achieve a diverse and supportive learning environment that sparks curiosity, builds confidence and enables every student to succeed in real-world, on the job settings. \u00a0 About You \u00a0 You are a passionate and experienced medical educator with a strong commitment to student success, teaching excellence and continuous improvement in higher education that is underpinned by your experience and expertise in hands-on simulated-focused learning. You bring demonstrated leadership in curriculum design, leadership and innovative teaching practices, alongside the ability to build meaningful relationships with students, colleagues and external partners. With a health professional background and a contemporary approach to learning and teaching, you are motivated to shape the next generation of healthcare professionals through excellence in education and collaboration. \u00a0 To be successful in this position, you also be able to demonstrate: Evidence of application of pedagogical theory and contemporary educational practice relevant to the discipline, in addition to substantial evidence of teaching at a tertiary level, inclusive of simulation and/or clinical setting. Demonstrated capacity to design and integrate clinical skills, clinical reasoning and patient assessment activities across curriculum. Relevant health professional qualification and current registration with the Australian Health Practitioner Regulation Agency (Ahpra). PHD, Tertiary Qualifications and/or equivalent professional experience in Health. \u00a0 College of Medicine and Public Health \u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 At the College of Medicine and Public Health, we deliver clinical, population and lab-based research, integrated teaching programs and high-quality clinical services. Our footprint reaches out from our world class teaching hospital at the Flinders Medical Centre in South Australia to multiple rural clinical locations all the way to Darwin in the Northern Territory. Our research and teaching equip the next generation of leaders and innovators with the skill, commitment, and vision to protect vulnerable communities and truly advance health outcomes. It is at the heart of everything we do. \u00a0 Life at Flinders \u00a0 They say know your place.\u00a0 We say you've found it right here. \u00a0 Flinders University was founded on the belief that learning should open minds, celebrate individuality and give people the freedom to pursue their own point of view. That spirit lives on in our community of thinkers, doers and changemakers who challenge convention, and each other, to shape what comes next. \u00a0 Rising to a challenge is nothing new for Flinders. During our first 60 years, we\u2019ve navigated revolutionary changes in social and cultural norms, and have responded to transformative economic, environmental and technological developments. Through it all, we\u2019ve continued to deliver for our students and community, innovating in learning and research to prepare graduates for the changing world they help create. \u00a0 Reaching beyond the limits of buildings, borders, and backgrounds, ours is an inclusive culture that believes absolutely in equality and opportunity for all. We don't just accommodate differences; we embrace and celebrate them. \u00a0 So, \u00a0 why work at Flinders? 17% Superannuation + salary packaging options Flexible working arrangements Awarded the AHEIA Higher Education Award for Workplace Culture Excellence due to our commitment to wellbeing through our Thriving@Flinders staff wellbeing program Wide range of professional development activities and services, including exclusive staff study offers\u00a0 We embrace diversity and promote equity and inclusion for all students and staff, as shown through our three SAGE Cygnet Awards. Vibrant campus life and amenities including on campus\u00a0 health care services ,\u00a0 gym \u00a0and\u00a0 childcare centre (Bedford Park, South Australia). Recognised as a Veteran Employer of Choice\u00a0 Our Commitment to Reconciliation and Indigenous Employment Flinders University is proud to be an organisation that is committed to our Reconciliation Action Plan and Indigenous Workforce Strategy. Our vision is to be a preferred employer for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples.\u00a0 We are committed to progressing Indigenous advancement in education, research, employment, and wellbeing, and strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all Flinders vacancies. Please see here for our Reconciliation Action Plan \u00a0 Please see here for our Indigenous Workforce Strategy \u00a0 Prescribed Conditions for Employment \u00a0 Appointment to this role is conditional on the completion of required pre-employment checks and declarations, each of which must be satisfactory to the University. \u00a0 These include: Flinders University will require a current completed Nationally Coordinated Criminal History Check and Gender Based Violence Declaration which is satisfactory to the University. The contract of Employment is conditional upon the receipt of these completed compliance checks. A disclosable outcome will not automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration. Each case will be assessed on its individual merits and relevance to the inherent requirements of the role. Staff working in a health care setting are strongly recommended to be fully vaccinated against COVID-19 in line with the SA Health policy. \u00a0 How to Apply and Information You are required to submit a CV, along with a Suitability Statement as a separate document. This should be no more than 3 pages and address the Key Position Capabilities of the position description. Flinders University is committed to providing an environment where staff with disability are valued, supported and encouraged to participate fully and independently in the life of the University.\u00a0If you require any reasonable adjustments to assist you in the selection process, please contact the Recruitment Team so that we can make appropriate arrangements through recruitment@flinders.edu.au or call 08 8201 2383. For more information regarding this position, please contact Fiona Wise . Certification Applications to be submitted before 10.00pm: 29 Oct 2026 At Flinders we embrace and celebrate diversity and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people of all ages, ethnicities, abilities, sexual orientations, and gender identities. Flinders. Fearless."}, "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Bedford-Park--Kaurna-Country/Change-Management-Lead_JR0000017780": {"title": "Change Management Lead", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nFull time\n\nPosition Details Full-Time | Fixed term until April 2029 Higher Education Officer Level 9 | $133,860 - $143,239 p.a. Location: Bedford Park / Kaurna Country View Position Description About the Flinders HealthCare Centre The Flinders HealthCARE Centre (FHC) is a multidisciplinary education, research, and healthcare facility located at the heart of Flinders Village and co-funded by the Australian Government and Flinders University. Scheduled to open in 2029, FHC will support the delivery of approximately 1,300 additional health graduates and up to 10,000 additional episodes of health and community care annually, bringing together education, research, and health and community services to enable new models of care, innovative use of technology, and transformative learning. About the Program\u00a0 The Program supports the establishment and activation of the FHC, working across the Colleges of Health and Enablement (CHE), Medicine and Public Health (CMPH), and Human Sciences and Culture (CHSC). With support from central services, the Activation team is structured across four workstreams and five enabling streams to support the design of an innovative interprofessional curriculum, underpinned by a newly defined clinical services model and contemporary simulation practices. The Program will also focus on co-designing health services in partnership with government and industry partners. About the Role Join us as our Change Management Lead for the activation of the Flinders HealthCare Centre, offering an exciting opportunity to be a part of a high performing project team who are shaping the development of the iconic, state of the art Flinders HealthCare Centre. Reporting to the Program Director, and working closely with the Associate Director, Change and Strategy, in the People and Culture portfolio, the Change Management Lead will ensure change strategies and plans align with the organisational objectives and the University's Change Management Framework. The incumbent will bring significant experience and sound knowledge in change management and communication, with the ability to foster cultural alignment during the transition into the new Flinders HealthCARE Centre building. The incumbent will lead change management programs and develop comprehensive plans to ensure the FHC Activation Program\u2019s change initiatives are successfully implemented. The role is also responsible for: Overseeing, gathering and analysing data, assessing the impact of change, recommending interventions and mitigations, and providing insights to help informed decision-marking. Creating and delivering tailored change management plans and required supporting plans such as Communications and Engagement Plans. Building and maintaining trusted relationships with key stakeholders, which includes providing guidance, addressing their needs and concerns, and assisting leaders to be the \u2018face of change\u2019 through practical and strategic change management techniques. Leading, delivering, and monitoring engagements to ensure regular, meaningful opportunities for stakeholders and impacted groups that enable buy-in, builds understanding, and support early adoption. Please refer to the attached position description, for a comprehensive list of roles and responsibilities. \u00a0 This position makes a significant contribution to the University\u2019s strategic plan to changing 10 million lives, Every One Matters, by 2035 through the strategic drive of Students First . This enabling role will play a pivotal role in the successful development and launch of the Flinders HealthCare Centre; a centre designed to offer modern, simulation training facilities that enhance student workforce readiness and strengthen their impact when entering communities as practitioners. \u00a0 About You You have highly developed interpersonal, and relationship management skills, with experience building and maintaining effective relationships with stakeholders and supporting individuals and groups through diverse types and levels of change. You bring a proven ability to lead and facilitate stakeholder engagement at all levels, develop high-quality communications, and oversee and deliver learning, readiness and adoption activities. You have excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to communicate clearly and effectively with diverse audiences, and extensive experience fostering flexible ways of working to drive collaboration, adaptability and successful outcomes. You will also be able to demonstrate: Postgraduate qualifications and extensive relevant experience, or an equivalent combination of experience and/or education and/or training. Experience in leading and delivering successful change management programs and services across entire project lifecycles. Extensive experience in overseeing and undertaking change impact analysis and creating fit-for-purpose change management plans for impacted groups. Experience in leading and overseeing project and change management resources to deliver change management activities. \u00a0 Life at Flinders \u00a0 They say know your place.\u00a0 We say you've found it right here. Flinders University was founded on the belief that learning should open minds, celebrate individuality and give people the freedom to pursue their own point of view. That spirit lives on in our community of thinkers, doers and changemakers who challenge convention, and each other, to shape what comes next. Rising to a challenge is nothing new for Flinders. During our first 60 years, we\u2019ve navigated revolutionary changes in social and cultural norms, and have responded to transformative economic, environmental and technological developments. Through it all, we\u2019ve continued to deliver for our students and community, innovating in learning and research to prepare graduates for the changing world they help create. Reaching beyond the limits of buildings, borders, and backgrounds, ours is an inclusive culture that believes absolutely in equality and opportunity for all. We don't just accommodate differences; we embrace and celebrate them. So, \u00a0 why work at Flinders? \u00a0 17% Superannuation + salary packaging options Flexible working arrangements Awarded the AHEIA Higher Education Award for Workplace Culture Excellence due to our commitment to wellbeing through our Thriving@Flinders staff wellbeing program Wide range of professional development activities and services, including exclusive staff study offers\u00a0 We embrace diversity and promote equity and inclusion for all students and staff, as shown through our three SAGE Cygnet Awards. Vibrant campus life and amenities including on campus\u00a0 health care services ,\u00a0 gym \u00a0and\u00a0 childcare centre (Bedford Park, South Australia). Recognised as a Veteran Employer of Choice\u00a0 \u00a0 Our Commitment to Reconciliation and Indigenous Employment \u00a0 Flinders University is proud to be an organisation that is committed to our Reconciliation Action Plan and Indigenous Workforce Strategy. Our vision is to be a preferred employer for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples.\u00a0 We are committed to progressing Indigenous advancement in education, research, employment, and wellbeing, and strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all Flinders vacancies. \u00a0 Please see here for our Reconciliation Action Plan \u00a0 Please see here for our Indigenous Workforce Strategy \u00a0 \u00a0 Prescribed Conditions for Employment \u00a0 Appointment to this role is conditional on the completion of required pre-employment checks and declarations, each of which must be satisfactory to the University. These include: \u00a0 Flinders University will require a current completed Nationally Coordinated Criminal History Check and Gender Based Violence Declaration which is satisfactory to the University. The contract of Employment is conditional upon the receipt of these completed compliance checks. A disclosable outcome will not automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration. Each case will be assessed on its individual merits and relevance to the inherent requirements of the role. SA: Staff working in a health care setting are strongly recommended to be fully vaccinated against COVID-19 in line with the SA Health policy. How to Apply and Information You are required to submit a CV, along with a Suitability Statement as a separate document.\u00a0 This should be no more than 3 pages, and address the Key Position Capabilities of the Position Description Flinders University is committed to providing an environment where staff with disability are valued, supported and encouraged to participate fully and independently in the life of the University.\u00a0If you require any reasonable adjustments to assist you in the selection process, please advise the contact in the Recruitment Team so that we can make appropriate arrangements through recruitment@flinders.edu.au or call 08 8201 2383. For more information regarding this position, please contact Dr Mailys Stirling Certification Applications to be submitted before 10.00pm: 01 Nov 2026 At Flinders we embrace and celebrate diversity and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people of all ages, ethnicities, abilities, sexual orientations, and gender identities. Flinders. Fearless."}, "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Bedford-Park--Kaurna-Country/Research-Assistant_JR0000017782": {"title": "Research Assistant", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nFull time\n\nPosition Details Part-time or Full-time Position (0.6FTE-1FTE) | Fixed Term until end of June 2027. Higher Education Officer Level 5 | $84,599 - $93,366 p.a. Location: Bedford Park / Kaurna Country View Position Description \u00a0 About the Role \u00a0 Join the National Centre for Education and Training on Addiction (NCETA) Research Team and contribute to the impactful research led by the internationally recognised Centre that works as a catalyst for change in the alcohol and other drugs field. Working closely as part of the wider Research Team, the Centre Director and government stakeholders, you will have the opportunity to support a variety of research activities imbedded in diverse projects. If you enjoy working collaboratively as part of a team on research and project-based tasks, we want to hear from you. Take a closer look at some of the everyday tasks you will have the opportunity to work on below: Assisting in capturing and sharing project outcomes and organisational Key Performance Indicators. Assisting with research ethics applications, grant applications and literature reviews. Maintaining spreadsheets, databases, EndNote libraries and maintaining accurate records of research procedures. Assisting with qualitative and quantitative data management, including data cleaning, coding, analysis, and summaries of findings. \u00a0 This position makes a significant contribution to the University\u2019s strategic plan to change 10 million lives, Every One Matters , by 2035, through directly contributing to the Strategic Driver of Research that Matters . This enabling role works to support innovative research with a goal of reducing the harms from alcohol and other drugs along the continuum from prevention through to treatment, to improve health outcomes for communities locally and globally. \u00a0 About You \u00a0 You are a proactive and detail-oriented research professional with a strong foundation in public health, health science or psychology, coupled with a passion for contributing to meaningful health research. Comfortable working both independently and as part of a multidisciplinary team, you bring excellent organisational skills, research rigour and a collaborative approach to supporting research projects from data collection through to reporting and communications. \u00a0 To be successful in this position, you will also bring: Completion of degree in relevant area (e.g. psychology, public health or science) or an equivalent combination of experience and/or education and/or training. Demonstrated well-developed writing and communication skills, particularly related to assisting in scientific manuscript preparation, industry reports, grant writing, or research dissemination (e.g. via newsletters, websites, social media). Well-developed qualitative and quantitative research skills. Well-developed computer skills including Microsoft Office products such as Word, Excel, and PowerPoint, statistical software (e.g., SPSS, R) and Endnote. \u00a0 College of Medicine and Public Health \u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0 At the College of Medicine and Public Health, we deliver clinical, population and lab-based research, integrated teaching programs and high-quality clinical services. Our footprint reaches out from our world class teaching hospital at the Flinders Medical Centre in South Australia to multiple rural clinical locations all the way to Darwin in the Northern Territory. Our research and teaching equip the next generation of leaders and innovators with the skill, commitment, and vision to protect vulnerable communities and truly advance health outcomes. It is at the heart of everything we do. \u00a0 Life at Flinders \u00a0 They say know your place.\u00a0 We say you've found it right here. \u00a0 Flinders University was founded on the belief that learning should open minds, celebrate individuality and give people the freedom to pursue their own point of view. That spirit lives on in our community of thinkers, doers and changemakers who challenge convention, and each other, to shape what comes next. \u00a0 Rising to a challenge is nothing new for Flinders. During our first 60 years, we\u2019ve navigated revolutionary changes in social and cultural norms, and have responded to transformative economic, environmental and technological developments. Through it all, we\u2019ve continued to deliver for our students and community, innovating in learning and research to prepare graduates for the changing world they help create. \u00a0 Reaching beyond the limits of buildings, borders, and backgrounds, ours is an inclusive culture that believes absolutely in equality and opportunity for all. We don't just accommodate differences; we embrace and celebrate them. \u00a0 So,\u00a0 why work at Flinders? 17% Superannuation + salary packaging options Flexible working arrangements Awarded the AHEIA Higher Education Award for Workplace Culture Excellence due to our commitment to wellbeing through our Thriving@Flinders staff wellbeing program Wide range of professional development activities and services, including exclusive staff study offers\u00a0 We embrace diversity and promote equity and inclusion for all students and staff, as shown through our three SAGE Cygnet Awards. Vibrant campus life and amenities including on campus\u00a0 health care services ,\u00a0 gym \u00a0and\u00a0 childcare centre (Bedford Park, South Australia). Recognised as a Veteran Employer of Choice\u00a0 Our Commitment to Reconciliation and Indigenous Employment Flinders University is proud to be an organisation that is committed to our Reconciliation Action Plan and Indigenous Workforce Strategy. Our vision is to be a preferred employer for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples. We are committed to progressing Indigenous advancement in education, research, employment, and wellbeing, and strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all Flinders vacancies. Please see here for our Reconciliation Action Plan \u00a0 Please see here for our Indigenous Workforce Strategy \u00a0 \u00a0 Prescribed Conditions for Employment \u00a0 Appointment to this role is conditional on the completion of required pre-employment checks and declarations, each of which must be satisfactory to the University. These include: Flinders University will require a current completed Nationally Coordinated Criminal History Check and Gender Based Violence Declaration which is satisfactory to the University. The contract of Employment is conditional upon the receipt of these completed compliance checks. A disclosable outcome will not automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration. Each case will be assessed on its individual merits and relevance to the inherent requirements of the role. Staff working in a health care setting are strongly recommended to be fully vaccinated against COVID-19 in line with the SA Health policy. \u00a0 How to Apply and Information You are required to submit a CV, along with a Suitability Statement as a separate document. This should be no more than 3 pages, and address each of the Key Position Capabilities of the position description. Flinders University is committed to providing an environment where staff with disability are valued, supported and encouraged, and can, as far as practicably possible, participate fully and independently in the life of the University.\u00a0If you require any reasonable adjustments to assist you in the selection process, including being accompanied by an accredited assistance animal with public access rights as per the Disability Policy , please advise the contact the Recruitment Team so that we can make appropriate arrangements through recruitment@flinders.edu.au or call 08 8201 2383. For more information regarding this position, please contact Sarah Powell. Certification Applications to be submitted before 10.00pm: 01 Nov 2026 At Flinders we embrace and celebrate diversity and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people of all ages, ethnicities, abilities, sexual orientations, and gender identities. Flinders. Fearless."}, "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Charles-Darwin-University-Darwin--Larrakia-Country/Operational-Support-Officer--Rural-and-Remote-Health_JR0000017372": {"title": "Operational Support Officer, Rural and Remote Health", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nFull time\n\nPosition Details Full time | Fixed term until 31 December 2027 Professional HEO5 | $84,599 - $93,366 Location: Darwin / Larrakia View Position Description \u00a0 About the Role \u00a0 We are seeking a proactive and highly organised Operational Support Officer to join the Operational Support team and deliver high quality operational and administrative support to the Discipline of Rural and Remote Health (RRH) at Flinders University. In this diverse role, you will be responsible for coordinating operational activities including conferences and events, stakeholder visits, while providing executive support to leadership staff. Based at the Darwin Casuarina campus, this position contributes to the ongoing improvements of operational procedures, administrative systems and work instructions to support consistent and effective service delivery across the discipline. \u00a0 Key responsibilities include: Providing operational and administrative support, including calendar management, coordination of meetings and conferences, and the preparation and distribution of correspondence. Building and maintaining effective working relationships with leadership staff and key stakeholders. Supporting the development and ongoing maintenance of operational procedures, processes and templates to support efficient and consistent service delivery. Coordinating travel arrangements for staff, students, visitors and groups, ensuring compliance with university policies and procedures. \u00a0 This position makes a significant contribution to the University\u2019s strategic plan, Changing Lives, Every One Matters , by 2035 through being collaborative, responsive and service-focused, supporting the University's commitment to the Core Enabler of Stronger Together and ensuring effective engagement with staff, students and stakeholders. \u00a0 About You \u00a0 You are a highly organised and proactive professional with experience providing operational and administrative support in a complex environment. With strong communication and stakeholder engagement skills, you thrive in a fast-paced setting, effectively managing competing priorities while delivering high-quality customer service and operational outcomes. You are solutions-focused, detail-oriented and committed to continuous improvement, with the ability to work both independently and collaboratively to support organisational goals. \u00a0 To be successful in this position, you will demonstrate: Proven experience providing operational and administrative support, including coordinating events, travel, facilities, resources and business operations within a complex organisation. Strong organisational and problem-solving skills, with the ability to manage competing priorities, meet deadlines and maintain a high level of accuracy and attention to detail. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to build positive relationships and work collaboratively with a diverse range of internal and external stakeholders. Sound knowledge of contemporary administrative systems, software and processes, with the ability to interpret and apply policies and procedures to support efficient service delivery and continuous improvement. \u00a0 Flinders Rural and Remote Health NT \u00a0 At Flinders Rural and Remote Health NT , our aim is to be a hub for innovative health research, education, and workforce development across the Northern Territory.\u00a0 We engage with students, community, and stakeholders to provide critical programs, such as the Northern Territory Medical Program, Paramedicine, Rural Clinical School, and the University Department of Rural Health. \u00a0 Our postgraduate education pathways (Remote Health Practice program), provides workforce development through Indigenous health and clinical skills training, and we have a community driven research program led by researchers committed to improving health outcomes. We work alongside Poche SA+NT focussing on Indigenous leadership capacity development and developing the Indigenous health workforce.\u00a0 All activities are driven by our values which focus on the long-term and short-term needs of the NT community. \u00a0 Life at Flinders \u00a0 They say know your place. We say you've found it right here. \u00a0 Flinders University was founded on the belief that learning should open minds, celebrate individuality and give people the freedom to pursue their own point of view. That spirit lives on in our community of thinkers, doers and changemakers who challenge convention, and each other, to shape what comes next. \u00a0 Rising to a challenge is nothing new for Flinders. During our first 60 years, we\u2019ve navigated revolutionary changes in social and cultural norms, and have responded to transformative economic, environmental and technological developments. Through it all, we\u2019ve continued to deliver for our students and community, innovating in learning and research to prepare graduates for the changing world they help create. \u00a0 Reaching beyond the limits of buildings, borders, and backgrounds, ours is an inclusive culture that believes absolutely in equality and opportunity for all. We don't just accommodate differences; we embrace and celebrate them. \u00a0 So, \u00a0 why work at Flinders? 17% Superannuation + salary packaging options Flexible working arrangements Awarded the AHEIA Higher Education Award for Workplace Culture Excellence due to our commitment to wellbeing through our Thriving@Flinders staff wellbeing program Wide range of professional development activities and services, including exclusive staff study offers\u00a0 We embrace diversity and promote equity and inclusion for all students and staff, as shown through our three SAGE Cygnet Awards. Recognised as a Veteran Employer of Choice\u00a0 Our Commitment to Reconciliation and Indigenous Employment \u00a0 Flinders University is proud to be an organisation that is committed to our Reconciliation Action Plan and Indigenous Workforce Strategy. Our vision is to be a preferred employer for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples.\u00a0 We are committed to progressing Indigenous advancement in education, research, employment, and wellbeing, and strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all Flinders vacancies. Please see here for our Reconciliation Action Plan \u00a0 Please see here for our Indigenous Workforce Strategy \u00a0 undefined Prescribed Conditions for Employment \u00a0 Appointment to this role is conditional on the completion of required pre-employment checks and declarations, each of which must be satisfactory to the University. \u00a0 These include: Flinders University will require a current completed Nationally Coordinated Criminal History Check and Gender Based Violence Declaration which is satisfactory to the University. The contract of Employment is conditional upon the receipt of these completed compliance checks. A disclosable outcome will not automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration. Each case will be assessed on its individual merits and relevance to the inherent requirements of the role. Staff working in a health care setting are required to be fully vaccinated against COVID-19 in line with the NT Health policy. Northern Territory Government legislation (the Care and Protection of Children Act 2007) now requires all individuals in child related employment or whose duties involve, or are likely to involve, contact with a child, to hold a valid 'Working with Children Clearance' (Ochre Card). This position involves child related work and is assessed as requiring a Working with Children Clearance/Ochre Card. undefined How to Apply and Information You are required to submit a CV, along with a Suitability Statement as a separate document.\u00a0 This should be no more than 3 pages and address the Key Position Capabilities of the position description . Candidates who have already applied for this position are not required to submit a new application. Flinders University is committed to providing an environment where staff with disability are valued, supported and encouraged to participate fully and independently in the life of the University.\u00a0If you require any reasonable adjustments to assist you in the selection process, please advise the contact in the Recruitment Team so that we can make appropriate arrangements through recruitment@flinders.edu.au or call 08 8201 2383. For more information regarding this position, please contact Amy Schulz. Certification Applications to be submitted before 10.00pm: 28 Oct 2026 At Flinders we embrace and celebrate diversity and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people of all ages, ethnicities, abilities, sexual orientations, and gender identities. Flinders. Fearless."}, "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Bedford-Park--Kaurna-Country/Lecturer-in-Critical-Indigenous-Studies--Identified-_JR0000017765": {"title": "Lecturer in Critical Indigenous Studies (Identified)", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nFull time\n\nPosition Details Full-Time | Teaching Specialist Continuing position Academic Level B | $115,871 - $137,122 pa Location: Bedford Park / Kaurna Country View Position Description Acknowledgement of Country: Flinders University acknowledges the Traditional Owners and Custodians of the lands on which its campuses are located. These are the Traditional Lands of the Arrernte, Dagoman, First Nations of the South East, First Peoples of the River Murray & Mallee region, Jawoyn, Kaurna, Larrakia, Ngadjuri, Ngarrindjeri, Ramindjeri, Warumungu, Wardaman and Yolngu people. We honour their Elders past, present and emerging. About the Role We are seeking a dedicated and forward-thinking Lecturer (Teaching Specialist) to contribute to student success and excellence in teaching and learning across undergraduate and postgraduate programs. With growing student enrolments and increasing demand across the Critical Indigenous Studies teaching portfolio, this position offers an opportunity to play a vital role in sustaining and strengthening the discipline and its interdisciplinary engagement across the University. You will contribute to high-quality teaching, curriculum development, topic coordination, assessment and student support, helping ensure positive student outcomes and an interdisciplinary and culturally responsive learning environment. This position will be predominantly concerned with teaching and teaching-related duties, with responsibilities including, but not limited to: Direct teaching informed by approaches that enhance the student experience; Curriculum design and review; Making an independent contribution to the review, renewal, development and design of curricula and courses that are attractive to existing and new cohorts of students and that nurture creativity and critical thinking skills; Providing support, academic counselling and professional advice to students concerning their studies, professional development and career opportunities. Working collaboratively across disciplines to deliver interdisciplinary learning experiences that enhance student engagement and success. The filling of this position is intended to constitute a special/equal opportunity measure under section 56 of the Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (SA) and Anti-Discrimination Act 1992 under section 35 (NT). The position is therefore only open to Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander people. The successful candidate will be required to provide Confirmation of Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander descent \u00a0 About You We are seeking an engaging and collaborative educator with a strong commitment to Critical Indigenous Studies and the delivery of culturally responsive, academically rigorous teaching. You must bring a student-centred approach to learning and a commitment to creating inclusive educational experiences that support student achievement, belonging and success. The successful candidate will demonstrate the following, among other capabilities: Experience of significant teaching and learning experience and excellence. Evidence of use of learning and teaching approaches which enhance student success. Evidence of successful and independent innovation in learning and teaching delivery or design, including use of e-learning technologies. About the College/Portfolio Through our world-class teaching and research, we equip students with the skill, commitment, and vision to protect vulnerable communities and advance human development. The College is dedicated to cultivating bright minds and inspiring innovative, passionate, and highly skilled graduates for future ready careers, and delivering connections for life.\u00a0 \u00a0 Life at Flinders They say know your place.\u00a0 We say you've found it right here. Flinders University was founded on the belief that learning should open minds, celebrate individuality and give people the freedom to pursue their own point of view. That spirit lives on in our community of thinkers, doers and changemakers who challenge convention, and each other, to shape what comes next. Rising to a challenge is nothing new for Flinders. During our first 60 years, we\u2019ve navigated revolutionary changes in social and cultural norms, and have responded to transformative economic, environmental and technological developments. Through it all, we\u2019ve continued to deliver for our students and community, innovating in learning and research to prepare graduates for the changing world they help create. Reaching beyond the limits of buildings, borders, and backgrounds, ours is an inclusive culture that believes absolutely in equality and opportunity for all. We don't just accommodate differences; we embrace and celebrate them.\u00a0 So, \u00a0 why work at Flinders? \u00a0 17% Superannuation + salary packaging options Flexible working arrangements Awarded the AHEIA Higher Education Award for Workplace Culture Excellence due to our commitment to wellbeing through our Thriving@Flinders staff wellbeing program Wide range of professional development activities and services, including exclusive staff study offers\u00a0 We embrace diversity and promote equity and inclusion for all students and staff, as shown through our three SAGE Cygnet Awards. Vibrant campus life and amenities including on campus\u00a0 health care services ,\u00a0 gym \u00a0and\u00a0 childcare centre (Bedford Park, South Australia). Recognised as a Veteran Employer of Choice\u00a0\u00a0 Our Commitment to Reconciliation and Indigenous Employment Flinders University is proud to be an organisation that is committed to our Reconciliation Action Plan and Indigenous Workforce Strategy. Our vision is to be a preferred employer for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples.\u00a0 We are committed to progressing Indigenous advancement in education, research, employment, and wellbeing, and strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all Flinders vacancies.\u00a0 Please see here for our Reconciliation Action Plan \u00a0 Please see here for our Indigenous Workforce Strategy \u00a0\u00a0 Prescribed Conditions for Employment \u00a0 Appointment to this role is conditional on the completion of required pre-employment checks and declarations, each of which must be satisfactory to the University. These include:\u00a0 Flinders University will require a current completed Nationally Coordinated Criminal History Check and Gender Based Violence Declaration which is satisfactory to the University. The contract of Employment is conditional upon the receipt of these completed compliance checks. A disclosable outcome will not automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration. Each case will be assessed on its individual merits and relevance to the inherent requirements of the role. In addition, it is a requirement of this position that the incumbent maintain a current Working With Children Check which is satisfactory to the University in accordance with the Child Safety (Prohibited Persons) Act 2016 (SA).\u00a0 How to Apply and Information You are required to submit a CV, along with a Suitability Statement as a separate document.\u00a0 This should be no more than 3 pages, and address the Key Position Capabilities of the position description . For more information regarding this position, please contact Azra Coombe . \u00a0 Applications to be submitted before 10:00 pm (ACDT) on Sunday, 1 November 2026. Please note, late applications and applications sent via agencies will not be accepted . At Flinders we embrace and celebrate diversity and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people of all ages, ethnicities, abilities, sexual orientations, and gender identities. Certification Applications to be submitted before 10.00pm: 01 Nov 2026 At Flinders we embrace and celebrate diversity and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people of all ages, ethnicities, abilities, sexual orientations, and gender identities. Flinders. Fearless."}}, "rows": {"https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Flinders-Rural-Health-SA-Mount-Gambier--On-the-Traditional-Lands-of-the-First-Nations-of-the-South-East/Casual-Professional-Academic-Register---Rural-and-Remote-Health-SA_JR0000011666-1": {"school_id": 1805, "posting_url": "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Flinders-Rural-Health-SA-Mount-Gambier--On-the-Traditional-Lands-of-the-First-Nations-of-the-South-East/Casual-Professional-Academic-Register---Rural-and-Remote-Health-SA_JR0000011666-1", "job_title_in_post": "Casual Professional/Academic Register \u2013 Rural and Remote Health SA", "position_type": "Non-academic", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "State's regional areas", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": "2026-03-02"}, "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Bedford-Park/Casual-Academic-Register---College-of-Business-Government-and-Law_JR0000000087": {"school_id": 1805, "posting_url": "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Bedford-Park/Casual-Academic-Register---College-of-Business-Government-and-Law_JR0000000087", "job_title_in_post": "Casual Academic Register \u2013 College of Business, Creative Arts, Law and Social Sciences", "position_type": "Non-academic", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "College of Business, Creative Arts, Law and Social Sciences", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": "2026-02-26"}, "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Bedford-Park/Casual-Academic-Register---College-o